\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk: Current Level Of Baht Won't Affect Exports \b0\par\par\uc2 199 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2000\par 09:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday that the current level of the baht won't adversely affect the country's exports. \par \par \uc2  Chetthavee Charoenpitaks, Bank of Thailand assistant governor for the Financial Markets \b \highlight22\uc2 Operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  Group, told reporters: "The baht at 37.40 to the dollar is okay." \par \par \uc2  "There should be no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I think in general this level shouldn't affect exports," he said. \par \par \uc2  At 0901 GMT (4:01 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted around THB37.367, down slightly from THB37.400 at the close of trading in Asia Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Chetthavee said the authorities shouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market because \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has abandoned the fixed exchange system. This means the baht has to move in line with market forces. \par \par \uc2  He said the recent movement of the baht in a range of two or three baht to the dollar "wasn't a great fluctuation." \par \par \uc2  He said investors should look at the baht with a longer term perspective. \par \par \uc2  "They shouldn't look at it on a day-to-day basis," he said. \par \par \uc2  -By Sinfah Tunsarawuth; 662-266-0744; sinfah.tunsarawuth@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw17004vv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
