\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht near 6-mth high late, sentiment improves. \b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2000\par 12:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1050 GMT - Thai baht\tab   rallies near six-month-high in late trade on Tuesday as sentiment in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  improved on expectations of capital inflow into the rallying equity market and eased Y2K concerns\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Baht 36.87/36.92 per dlr late vs 37.08/37.13 early Tuesday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  - Baht 37.8212/37.8873 per euro vs 37.8442/37.9837 \par \par \uc2  - Thai unit traded at 36.67 on July 6. \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Jan 4 (Reuters) - Thai baht rallied further against the dollar in late trade on Tuesday, nearing again a six-month high of 36.67 per dollar recorded on July 6. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Thai unit was supported by improved sentiment as the market anticipated foreign capital inflows linked to corporate investments in Thailand and into a surging domestic equity market. \par \par \uc2  Thai stocks closed sharply higher on Tuesday. The SET index ended up 3.43 percent at 498.46 in active trade. \par \par \uc2  "I think the money market has returned to normal after it had been plagued by Y2K anxiety throughout the last month," said a dealer at a major U.S. bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the baht'ss gain was in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Philippine peso and Indonesian rupiah. \par \par \uc2  The baht was also underpinned by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statement that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to influence the baht's movement despite its sharp rise. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also reiterated that it would allow the baht to fluctuate according to market forces. \par \par \uc2  "We would like to confirm that we will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and will let (the baht) move according to market forces. If we take any action, it would probably add to the baht's volatility, something which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not want to see," said assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chettavee Charoenpitaks. \par \par \uc2  One-month onshore baht/dollar swap discounts were quoted at -12.00/-10.00 satang against -13.50/-10.50 satang amid excess liquidity. \par \par \uc2  Offshore premiums were unchanged at 0.0/+2.0 satang. \par \par \uc2  The overnight interbank rate was at 0.75-1.0 pct. \par \par \uc2  ((Bangkok Newsroom +66-2 637 5500 ext 417 \par \par \uc2  email:bangkok.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dw1401j5e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
