\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Up on stock flows, authorities alert. \b0\par\par\uc2 986 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2000\par 09:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, Jan 4 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar\tab     shot\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more than two percent higher by Tuesday afternoon, providing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  the region's best example of capital inflows translating into \par \par \uc2  firmer \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the new year. \par \par \uc2      Impressive performances were made by many of Asian stock \par \par \uc2  markets on relief the Y2K bug had been a non-event, \par \par \uc2  underpinning the generally buoyant mood in almost all the \par \par \uc2  regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The speed of the rise in the yen\tab    , the Korean won and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Taiwan dollar proved too much for domestic authorities,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with dealers citing a flurry of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  activity aimed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at tempering further upside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dollar/yen bounced back above 102 after repeated rounds of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of Japan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lifted it off earlier lows of around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 101.46.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Offshore dollar sales as investors bought into a domestic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stock rally pushed the Taiwan dollar more than two and a half\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent higher despite efforts by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to steady\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its speedy rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The local unit soared as high as 30.53 per dollar,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par surpassing its recent string of 25-month highs around the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par T$31.39 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Taipei dealers said the government appeared more willing to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tolerate its appreciation of late due to an upturn in exports\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and as presidential elections were around the corner.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But an analyst at a U.S. bank in Singapore said the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government was likely to cap any rise above the 30.00 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Excitement over equities also fuelled sharp moves in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par won, forcing the monetary authorities to issue warnings and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par then follow through with dollar buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But renewed efforts to put the brakes on were short-lived,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the won swinging yet higher and ending at its strongest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level since late November 1997.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said a drop in exports caused by a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would not be desirable for economic recovery\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and that the monetary authorities would use various methods to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stabilise the domestic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht was slightly off after shooting higher in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offshore trade the previous day, but it was still trading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around its highest levels for six months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Thailand said the rise stemmed from optimism\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over foreign capital inflows linked to corporate investment and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a surging stock market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market to influence the baht's movement despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sharp rise and that it would allow it to fluctuate according to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market forces.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The consumer price index for 1999 rose 0.3 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year-on-year compared to an 8.1 percent year-on-year rise in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1998 while the wholesale price index (WPI) fell 6.5 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The WPI had risen 13.8 percent year-on-year in 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar gained almost half a percent despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corrective losses in the Straits Times Index\tab     after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par record closings over the past three sessions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said its upward bias was likely to continue based\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on better than expected growth data for the fourth quarter of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1999 and forecasts of sound growth ahead.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Some local analysts have said they see the STI heading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par towards 2,700 points by late January from around 2,500 now and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that dollar/Sing should reach between 1.50 to 1.60 by the end\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso gained as banks unloaded their dollar positions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par amid fading fears of the millennium bug.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Export growth looks set to rise steadily this year due to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par demand for electronic products in Asia and Europe. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government said exports rose 19 percent year-on-year in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par first 11 months of 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Finance Secretary Edgardo Espiritu said the benchmark\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 91-day Treasury bill rate could drop 25 basis points at next\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week's auction. It was at 8.898 percent at the last auction in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He also said annual inflation in December may come in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par higher than the November figure of 3.9 percent, a 12-year low,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but it should not exceed 4.5 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Reuters poll produced an average forecast of a 4.35\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent rise in December inflation. The number is due on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah was off its lows but still comfortably within\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 7,000/7,100 per dollar range in light trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's financial woes remained a focal point,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with dealers saying the published audit into its affairs would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be positive over the long term despite some immediate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bearishness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The IMF said Bank Indonesia needed some recapitalisation,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but there was nothing in the critical audit which showed the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank could not meet its daily obligations. It also said greater\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par transparency would strengthen BI.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A finance ministry official said the government would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unveil its next budget and the latest IMF letter of intent on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par January 20.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0801 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     102.88\tab  101.77\tab    -1.08\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6500\tab  1.6580\tab    +0.48\par  Taiwan dlr     30.57\tab   31.33\tab    +2.49\par  Korean won   1126.00\tab 1127.00\tab    +0.09\par  Baht\tab      36.86\tab   36.78\tab    -0.22\par  Peso\tab      39.76\tab   39.97\tab    +0.53\par  Rupiah\tab  7035.00\tab 7050.00\tab    +0.21\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7998\tab  3.7995\tab    -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     102.88\tab  102.21\tab    -0.65\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6500\tab  1.6640\tab    +0.85\par  Taiwan dlr     30.57\tab   31.38\tab    +2.65\par  Korean won   1126.00\tab 1135.00\tab    +0.80\par  Baht\tab      36.86\tab   37.45\tab    +1.60\par  Peso\tab      39.76\tab   40.20\tab    +1.11\par  Rupiah\tab  7035.00\tab 6975.00\