\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW - Thai c.bank says baht speculation curbed. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Rajan Moses \par \uc2 758 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 1999\par 11:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Dec 21 (Reuters) - Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Tuesday that "pure speculation" in the baht had now been curbed but remaining controls on baht transactions involving offshore players would still be kept. \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol Sonakul also told Reuters in a rare interview that although the baht was now relatively strong the Bank of Thailand was not propping up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There's no plan to do such a thing (lifting remaining controls). We can do it when the financial stabilising system comes out with a workable system where international capital flows can be...reasonable," he said. \par \par \uc2  A key remaining restriction on baht transactions for foreign parties is a 50 million baht limit on non-commercial swap deals. \par \par \uc2  The baht was quoted at around 37.85/37.95 to the U.S. dollar on Tuesday afternoon against 41.65 late in September. \par \par \uc2  "We are not actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all at this particular point. It is where people expect it to be given the trade and the FDI (foreign direct investment). \par \par \uc2  "FDI flow has been regular although not extensive as yet. (You've got to watch) the FDI coming in and making it (the baht) too strong. Otherwise it will actually neutralise the FDI coming in in terms of the exchange effects," he said. \par \par \uc2  But the governor said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again as it did in October to prevent sharp speculative baht movements. \par \par \uc2  "If you look at the Asia and Pacific baht rate, it is basically the same as the onshore baht rate. So the measures were successful," Chatu Mongol said. \par \par \uc2  NO NEW PROBE NEEDED AT KRUNG THAI BANK \par \par \uc2  He also said he did not think the government needed to conduct a new probe into debt-laden state-owned Krung Thai Bank Plc, at the centre of a controversy over its bad loans and management. \par \par \uc2  "Krung Thai is already being supervised full-time (by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," he said. The bank's non-performing loans stood at 51 percent of all loans at end-September and it accounts for nearly 20 percent share of all loans in the Thai banking sector. \par \par \uc2  Critics have been raking the government and in particular Finance Minister Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda for the handling of the bank. \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol said Krung Thai had not performed much worse than other Thai banks and actually faced more stringent supervision from the authorities, including the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other government auditors. \par \par \uc2  "We don't need to make Krung Thai the best Thai bank, just make it viable and fairly reasonable," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said he did not believe Krung Thai executives had been involved in questionable lending or fraudulent bank practices. \par \par \uc2  "All these cases will be very grey and some technical...involving some minor breaches of regulations. We are not going to have a case in which a guy stole a lot of money and ran away with it in a jeep," he said. \par \par \uc2  NON-PERFORMING LOANS STILL HIGH BUT DECLINING MONTHLY \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol said non-performing loans (NPLs) were still high, but were declining at a net rate of one percentage point per month. \par \par \uc2  "NPLs are coming down. Net wise, it is going down about one percentage point a month. The buying off of bank NPLs by the government also helped bring down the NPL figures," he said. \par \par \uc2  At end-October, there were 2.46 trillion baht (US$65 billion) of NPLs in the ailing financial system. The level of NPLs in the financial sector stood at around 43.8 percent of outstanding loans and 43.4 percent for banks alone. \par \par \uc2  At their peak at end May, NPLs in the whole financial sector were at 47.7 percent of total lending. \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol said the mechanism for dealing with NPLs was working well, but the authorities were still short of staff and expertise for monitoring the exact level of bank NPLs. \par \par \uc2  He said there was no policy conflict between himself and the finance minister as speculated recently in the local media. \par \par \uc2  The outspoken \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor also said he was keeping his options open on whether or not to enter politics. \par \par \uc2  "My career in politics will be based solely on whether there will be anything useful (for me) to do," he said. \par \par \uc2  The six-party coalition government of Prime Minister Chuan Leekpai must call an election by November but the beginnings of election fever are already starting to grip the country. \par \par \uc2  (US$1 = 38 baht). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvcl07rd3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
