\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht down on regionals, profit-taking sales. \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 1999\par 13:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1040 GMT - Thai baht\tab   sheds early gains as foreign players sell the unit and other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to take short-term profits\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Baht 38.82/38.886 per dlr vs 38.62/38.65\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  * Baht 41.2230/41.3125 per euro vs 40.8427/40.9149 \par \par \uc2  * Y 103.93/104.03 per dlr vs 104.01/104.06 \par \par \uc2  * One-month forward swap discounts -9.90/8.90 satangs onshore. Offshore premium-1.00/1.50 satangs \par \par \uc2  * Overnight interbank rate 1.25 to 1.375 pct \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  one-day repurchase rate 0.6875 pct. \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Oct 27 (Reuters) - The Thai baht lost ground against the dollar in late Asian trade on Wednesday as foreigners sold the unit to take profits after recent gains. \par \par \uc2  "I think the baht moved up a bit too fast (during the past few days)," said Satian Tantanasarit, senior vice president of DBS Thai Danu Bank. \par \par \uc2  The baht move was line with other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and with predictions by dealers that the unit would fall back after it failed to break beyond resistance at the 38.50 per dollar level. \par \par \uc2  The baht was seen heading towards support at 39 per dollar, while resistance remained at 38.50, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul said on Wednesday the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the baht in recent days. \par \par \uc2  The governor told reporters the baht's recent recovery, from 39.75 on October 11 and a 13-month low of about 41.70 in late September, had probably been helped by improved exports last month. \par \par \uc2  "On the baht strength, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still has not done anything. We have seen some foreign capital inflow as September exports increased and some people have unwound their (dollar) positions," he said. \par \par \uc2  ((Ekarin Petsiri, Bangkok Newsroom +66-2 637 5500 ext 417 \par \par \uc2  email:bangkok.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvar01cvj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
