\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk/Limit-3:Bid Direct Investment Inflows-Dep PM \b0\par\par\uc2 440 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 1999\par 15:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said the change was causing a severe short-squeeze for offshore investors who needed to cover short-term baht obligations. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar plunged to THB39.50 at the close of Asian trade Tuesday, from THB40.425 the previous day. \par \par \uc2  At 1252 GMT, the dollar was being quoted offshore in European and early U.S. trade at THB39.040. \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol said the baht's rise in Asian trade Tuesday was "not too fast" for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets only to counter speculative activity or to damp volatility, preventing the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from moving too far, too quickly. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok-based dealers said the dollar could open in Asian trade Wednesday as low as THB38.50, depending on how much short-term baht offshore investors have borrowed. \par \par \uc2  Deputy Premier Supachai Panitchpakdi told reporters after a late cabinet meeting Tuesday that the baht has recovered some of its recent losses because local companies who were rushing to pay down yen-denominated debts realize that the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stabilized. \par \par \uc2  The dollar appears to have settled in a range of Y105-Y110, while against the baht the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has retreated from a 13-month low last week around THB41.70. \par \par \uc2  Supachai said Thailand's economic prospects will show a lot of improvement by the end of the year, which should contribute to support for the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen since the latest Bank of Thailand indicators were released last week. \par \par \uc2  August export growth of 15% on the year and manufacturing production growth of 17.7% on the year showed the economic recovery is underway, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The deputy premier, who is also commerce minister, said foreign direct investment inflows are also very strong this year, and should reach $6 billion, compared with $3 billion to $5 billion a year in the last few years. \par \par \uc2  If the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can sell three more nationalized banks this year as planned, foreign confidence and the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will receive an even bigger boost, he said. \par \par \uc2  Thailand sold the nationalized Nakornthon Bank PCL (H.NKB) last month to the U.K.'s Standard Chartered, and will announce a deal for Radanasin Bank PCL (H.RDB) with Singapore's United Overseas Bank Ltd. (P.UOB) on Wednesday at 1100 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Two more nationalized banks are to be sold later this year. Short-lists of investors are currently under consideration. \par \par \uc2  -By Thomas Fox; 662-266-0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-10-99 \par \par \uc2  1319GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dva5079ns\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
