\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -3: Resurgent Economy To Buoy Thai Baht \b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 1999\par 10:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Maya Pinto, regional economist at IDEA Global.com, expects the U.S. dollar to continue to languish against the baht. \par \par \uc2  "Thai government comments are consistently baht-supportive, so we see the U.S. dollar at THB40 or even lower," she said, adding that any Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only be to smooth any sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements. \par \par \uc2  Pinto also said ratings agency Moody's Investors Service Inc. has sent analysts to Thailand to reassess the country's resurgent economy. "That could mean a possible upgrade, which would also be baht-supportive," she said. \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine dealing system, the U.S. dollar was trading at 40.7050 pesos, down from PHP40 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  In North Asia, the U.S. dollar is trading at 1,216 won, almost unchanged from KRW1,215.9 late the previous day. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar is also trading at NT$31.779, almost flat from NT31.778 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Desmond Supple, regional economist at Barclays Bank in Singapore, said the New Taiwan dollar has showed resistance to the financial aftershock of the recent earthquake. \par \par \uc2  He said the economic damage has been less than expected. \par \par \uc2  "As the dust, quite literally, clears, it is apparent that the export industry was far less affected than was initially thought," he said, in his daily market report. "Leading export-oriented electronics companies reported only several days of production delay, while even the worst affected sectors anticipate 80% capacity within a few weeks." \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's need to provide ample liquidity to the financial system has placed downward pressure on the New Taiwan dollar, but he believes it has been oversold. \par \par \uc2  "The earthquake is not expected to lead to significant New Taiwan dollar depreciation over the short term," he said, adding that he advises short U.S. dollar positions, as he expects the U.S. dollar to fall toward NT31.00 in the short term. \par \par \uc2  -By Brian Truscott; 65 421 4800; brian.truscott@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 01-10-99 \par \par \uc2  0846GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dva10758v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
