\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Stronger In Line With Regional  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 1999\par 13:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended stronger against the U.S. dollar in Asian spot trade midday Thursday in line with the dollar's move against other Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said volatility in the baht and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was lessening ahead of the release next week of a quarterly tankan business sentiment survey in Japan on Monday, and a U.S. Federal Open Market Committee meeting Tuesday. A positive report from Japan and a decision not to raise U.S. interest rates could lead to further upward pressure on the yen. \par \par \uc2  The yen's strength has been a factor in the baht's recent weakness, as companies have scrambled to pay down yen-denominated debt. But analysts expect outflows for debt repayment to slow with the end of the third quarter Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at THB41.14, down from THB41.245 at the close of trade in Bangkok Wednesday, and sharply lower than Wednesday's 13-month intraday high of THB41.68. \par \par \uc2  Investors began to take profits on dollar gains Wednesday, following comments by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials and the government's economic team, who said the country's economic fundamentals pointed to a baht level of under THB40 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Although the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to set the level of the baht, it has entered the market this week to stem excessive fluctuation in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The trading range narrowed Thursday, as players chased the dollar chased up and down a narrow range between THB40.95 and THB41.10 five times over the course of the day, they said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is expected to open Friday between strong support at THB40.75 and resistance at THB41.20. \par \par \uc2  -By Thomas Fox; 662 266 0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 30-09-99 \par \par \uc2  1110GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9u0768f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
