\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Regains Ground To End Steady On Dep PM Comment \b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 1999\par 12:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended steady against the U.S. dollar Wednesday, rallying from new lows in late Asian trade after the deputy prime minister said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was undervalued at present levels, given the country's economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Supachai Panitchpakdi told reporters in Singapore that the present state of Thailand's economy means a range of 37-38 baht to the dollar would be more appropriate. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished Wednesday at THB41.245, down from THB41.335 at Tuesday's Asian close, and lower than intraday highs that tested THB41.70. \par \par \uc2  Offshore investors who had bet on further baht declines through long-dollar positions liquidated those positions late Wednesday after Supachai indicated the baht should be stronger, a local trader said. \par \par \uc2  Investors were locking in profits on the dollar's recent strong gains amid a growing perception the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be running out of steam. \par \par \uc2  "We had real profit-taking there (at THB41.65)," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stem the baht's fall is also adding to the feeling the dollar can't go much higher, the trader said. Other traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold dollars Wednesday, but there was no confirmation. \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol Sonakul, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, said Tuesday in Washington that he's comfortable with the baht at THB41-THB42 to the dollar, although the bank would support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it fell too sharply. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says this isn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , adding it's happy for the market to set the actual level of the baht. Analysts say a weak baht helps exports by making them cheaper in terms of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But most traders agree the dollar-baht could actually get stronger in the near term, although at a slower pace than over the past few weeks. \par \par \uc2  Capital outflows from the stock market, repayment of foreign debt and a decision not to take the remaining money from an International Monetary Fund credit line could all hurt the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Exporters have also failed to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , remaining on the sidelines in anticipation of further baht weakness before they bring foreign profits back home. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Wright; 662 266 0744; thomas.wright@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 29-09-99 \par \par \uc2  1019GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9t072w0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
