\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -2: US Dollar Seen Rising To THB43 \b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 1999\par 10:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  At 0750 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at 8,485 rupiah, almost unchanged from IDR8,486 late Monday. Traders said the extremely thin, choppy market amplified moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with small U.S. dollar or rupiah orders placing undue pressure on pricing. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was also trading at 41.2650 baht, up from THB40.7350 Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said late Monday that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Friday to quell volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations. The bank's governor, Tanya Sirivedhin, said a range of THB41.00 to THB42.00 against the U.S. dollar is acceptable to authorities, but added the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if the baht becomes unacceptably weak. \par \par \uc2  Desmond Supple, regional economist at Barclays Bank in Singapore, sees the U.S. dollar actually strengthening to THB43.0 because he expects the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  - along with other regional banks - to further ease monetary policy for the remainder of the year. \par \par \uc2  "Regional central banks have leeway to ease monetary policy going forward, implying that asset markets will be more supported than Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the near term," he said. \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine Dealing System, the U.S. dollar was trading at 40.943 pesos, up from PHP40.73 in late Asian trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  Padgett said that for the moment, countries such as the Philippines and Thailand are experiencing a lull in foreign capital inflows. He said many overseas fund portfolios are now fully invested in regional markets, following the frenzied buying activity earlier in the year. \par \par \uc2  "That has run its course, but as further signs of economic growth arise and, in some case, political resolutions are made, there will ultimately be renewed pressure on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investment returns," he said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 28-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0836GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9s073qo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
