\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Lose Luster As US Dlr Rises Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 1999\par 03:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened generally weaker against the U.S. dollar in early trading Tuesday, thanks to U.S. gains against the yen in overnight trading. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar managed to climb as high as Y106.22 overnight, from an intraday low of Y103.92 Monday. Traders ascribed the climb to a residual effect from a weekend Group-of-Seven industrialized countries meeting in the U.S., where Japan said it will to provide ample market liquidity to cap yen strength. \par \par \uc2  At 0040 GMT (8:40 p.m. Monday EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y105.85. \par \par \uc2  Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets welcomed the news Monday, although overnight gains by the U.S. dollar damped the exuberance. Traders expect most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally to move sideways against the U.S. dollar during Tuesday's session. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht continues to be the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to watch, they said. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said late Monday that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Friday to quell volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations. The bank's governor, Tany Sirivedhin, said a range of 41 baht to THB42 against the U.S. dollar is acceptable to authorities, but added the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if the baht became unacceptably weak. \par \par \uc2  Traders said market liquidity is now a key factor. "It is struggling a little this morning, with resistance at the THB41 level," said a trader at a U.S. bank in Singapore. He expects the U.S. dollar to move between THB40.70 and THB41.20 during the session. \par \par \uc2  At 0050 GMT, the U.S. dollar was trading at THB40.925, up from THB40.7350 in late Asian trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading against the Singapore dollar at S$1.7040, just up from $1.7038 Monday. \par \par \uc2  Against the Indonesian rupiah, the U.S. dollar, in choppy, volatile trading, was quoted at IDR8,435, down a touch from IDR8,486 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine dealing system, the U.S. dollar was trading at 40.71 pesos, almost unchanged from PHP40.72 Monday. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the U.S dollar was quoted against the New Taiwan dollar at NT31.793, steady from late Monday's NT31.795. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was trading versus the Korean won at KRW1,210.6, hardly changed from KRW1,210.8 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Brian Truscott; 65 421 4800; brian.tuscott@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 28-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0108GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9s07287\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
