\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals droop, yen softens. \b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 1999\par 03:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0144 GMT - Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly easier in early \par \par \uc2  trade, with the yen's softer stance fuelling the impact of a \par \par \uc2  spate of domestic factors. \par \par \uc2      The dollar was off its highs above the 106 yen level but \par \par \uc2  still holding on to some of its overnight gains after European \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) Vice President Christian Noyer said the ECB \par \par \uc2  would be willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to maintain \par \par \uc2  stability. \par \par \uc2  Separately, New York Fed President William McDonough said: \par \par \uc2  "it impresses me that the G7 statement was very sound and Japan \par \par \uc2  has made a very clear statement in my view of what their \par \par \uc2  intentions are. That is a very positive step. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said dollar/yen was seen trading in a range \par \par \uc2  of 103 to 108 and that it would have to reach the 100 level \par \par \uc2  before the Bank of Japan felt pressured to act. \par \par \uc2  *** The Thai baht edged below the 41.0 per dollar level, \par \par \uc2  with players wary over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves to push it \par \par \uc2  higher. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said levels of 41-42 per dollar were \par \par \uc2  acceptable and suggested it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the baht fell \par \par \uc2  too far. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Tanya Sirivedhin said, "If \par \par \uc2  the baht is too weak and at an inappropiate level, then we will \par \par \uc2  take care of it." \par \par \uc2  The government released data showing Thai banks had reduced \par \par \uc2  their non-performing loans (NPLs) for the second consecutive \par \par \uc2  month in July, but analysts said the decline was too small to \par \par \uc2  improve market sentiment. \par \par \uc2      *** The peso took its cue from the baht, hovering at around \par \par \uc2  40 per dollar. \par \par \uc2      Manila traders said it had been moving in line with the \par \par \uc2  baht recently as the two countries' export markets were in \par \par \uc2  direct competition with each other. \par \par \uc2      *** The Taiwan dollar pared early losses and dealers \par \par \uc2  expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep it stable as the stock market \par \par \uc2  continued to come under pressure after last week's earthquake. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to support the Taiwan dollar in \par \par \uc2  late Monday trade and said it expected the island's sound \par \par \uc2  fundamentals to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Taipei stocks lost some 2.73 percent in early trade as \par \par \uc2  local investors continued to sell, but brokers said signs of \par \par \uc2  strong foreign fund buying offered some support. \par \par \uc2      *** The won opened lower, with dealers eyeing strong \par \par \uc2  support for the dollar at 1,210. \par \par \uc2      Seoul dealers said they expected dollar demand from foreign \par \par \uc2  stock investors who were seen translating their stock sales \par \par \uc2  into dollars. \par \par \uc2      *** The rupiah was barely changed as investors remained \par \par \uc2  sidelined by a slew of political uncertainties like East Timor, \par \par \uc2  political protests in the capital and the Bank Bali scandal. \par \par \uc2      But there were no market moving developments there, with \par \par \uc2  Jakarta still looking quiet after last week's bloody riots. \par \par \uc2      Student threats to march on parliament on Monday did not \par \par \uc2  materialise but they have plans to protest over a new security \par \par \uc2  law later in the week. \par \par \uc2       Change on the day TUE 28 0143GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000..........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8520.00......8350.00.........-2.00% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........41.14........40.74.........-0.97% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........40.94........40.67.........-0.66% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7055.......1.7026.........-0.17% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...31.750.......31.755..........0.02% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1210.80......1210.70.........-0.01% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....105.69.......104.37.........-1.25% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8520.00......2432.00........-71.46% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........41.16........25.90........-37.07% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........40.94........26.50........-35.27% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7055.......1.4300........-16.15% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr..31.7500......27.7500........-12.60% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1210.80.......842.00........-30.46% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....105.69.......114.40..........8.24% \par \par \uc2      ((Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3840;fax (65) 870-3787; email: \par \par \uc2  asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokume