\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk/Baht -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  Fri To Damp Volatility \b0\par\par\uc2 128 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 1999\par 13:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to defend the baht the previous Friday to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from fluctuating too much in a single day, not because the baht was too weak. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand Deputy Governor Tanya Sirivedhin said a range of THB41 to THB42 baht to the dollar was acceptable to authorities, but that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if the baht became "unacceptably weak." She declined to be more specific. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit a 13-month high Friday of THB41.41, before easing to an Asian close last week at THB41.215, and Monday at THB40.745. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 27-09-99 \par \par \uc2  1158GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9r0705g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
