\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals buoyed as yen bounces back. \b0\par\par\uc2 896 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 1999\par 11:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0920 GMT - Most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ticked higher in late \par \par \uc2  trade as the yen bounced back to around 104 to the dollar amid \par \par \uc2  waning hopes Japan would succeed in taming its rise. \par \par \uc2      The yen was squarely back to levels it enjoyed prior to a \par \par \uc2  weekend G7 statement, which expressed concern over the \par \par \uc2  potential impact of the strong yen on the global economy and \par \par \uc2  triggered rumours the Bank of Japan (BOJ) might ease credit. \par \par \uc2  Initial optimism over the statement soon gave way to \par \par \uc2  caution, with some dealers saying the market was looking for \par \par \uc2  concrete evidence of a change in monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  *** The rupiah firmed back above the 8,400 level as Jakarta \par \par \uc2  returned to normal after last week's bloody riots but dealers \par \par \uc2  said trade was thin and players cautious. \par \par \uc2  Student groups in the capital have vowed to protest until \par \par \uc2  the country's new security law - which they say will give the \par \par \uc2  military freer reign to crush dissent - is revoked. \par \par \uc2  They say the government's decision to delay its \par \par \uc2  implementation is insufficient and reject arguments that the \par \par \uc2  new law is better than the old one. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta dealers said the rupiah adopted a firmer tone after \par \par \uc2  parliament said that seven top officials, including the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor and finance minister, should face swift legal \par \par \uc2  action over the Bank Bali scandal. \par \par \uc2  The recent suspension of fresh loans by the International \par \par \uc2  Monetary Fund remained in place, though, as the IMF awaited the \par \par \uc2  release of an external audit on the bank. \par \par \uc2  The state statistics bureau said it expected September's \par \par \uc2  month-on-month inflation figure to be between minus 0.5 and \par \par \uc2  minus 0.9 percent, compared to minus 0.9 percent in August. \par \par \uc2  *** The Taiwan dollar pared early losses as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to protect it from the impact of last week's \par \par \uc2  earthquake, which killed some 2,100 people. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said damage to infrastructure and industry \par \par \uc2  was limited and economic recovery would be swift. \par \par \uc2      It said Taiwan's sound economic fundamentals would \par \par \uc2  stabilise the local dollar. \par \par \uc2      Taiwan shares fared worse, losing 2.66 percent on the first \par \par \uc2  trading day since the earthquake last Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      Newly narrowed volatility limits and buying of shares in \par \par \uc2  the construction sector cushioned the drop, but brokers \par \par \uc2  expected more declines. \par \par \uc2      *** The baht gained over one percent on the day as players \par \par \uc2  took profit on the dollar's surge to 13-month highs last week. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Singapore said players were also keen to cut \par \par \uc2  their dollar positions amid rumours the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forward market late on Friday. \par \par \uc2      But concerns about the level of non-performing loans \par \par \uc2  persisted, with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul \par \par \uc2  sounding a word of warning at the weekend. \par \par \uc2      Chatu said that NPLs were one reason to remain cautious \par \par \uc2  over Thailand although he expected the proportion of bad loans \par \par \uc2  to fall within the next few months due to measures taken by the \par \par \uc2  government and because of debtor-creditor agreements. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday that total NPLs of Thai \par \par \uc2  banks amounted to 46.12 percent of total credits at end-July \par \par \uc2  against 46.48 percent a month earlier. \par \par \uc2      *** The peso was firmer in line with the baht, but its rise \par \par \uc2  was blocked by corporate dollar bids near the 40.50 level. \par \par \uc2      The benchmark 91-day Treasury bill rate was almost flat at \par \par \uc2  8.548 percent at Monday's regular auction against 8.55 percent \par \par \uc2  last week. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday that it would not change \par \par \uc2  key overnight rates for now despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent falls \par \par \uc2  to 10-month lows. \par \par \uc2      The overnight borrowing rate would remain at an official \par \par \uc2  nine percent and overnight lending at 11 percent. \par \par \uc2      *** The Korean won lost ground as trade resumed after the \par \par \uc2  four-day Chusok holiday. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said it was depressed by dollar demand for foreign \par \par \uc2  debt payments, which offset the impact of some export deals. \par \par \uc2      Local banks plan to repay $8.75 billion in foreign loans in \par \par \uc2  early October. The loans were rolled over last year. \par \par \uc2      *** The Singapore dollar was slightly firmer. \par \par \uc2      Volume in Singapore's electronics output rose 33.6 percent \par \par \uc2  in August compared with the same month a year earlier. \par \par \uc2      The country's total manufacturing output climbed 18.4 \par \par \uc2  percent year-on-year in August, led by growth in the \par \par \uc2  electronics and chemical sectors. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day MON 27 0923GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8350.00......8640.00.........3.47% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........40.70........41.17.........1.15% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........40.67........40.88.........0.52% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7023.......1.7072.........0.29% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...31.755.......31.680........-0.24% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1210.70......1212.00.........0.11% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....104.66.......104.47........-0.18% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8350.00......2432.00........-70.87% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........40.70........25.90........-36.36% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........40.67........26.50........-34.84% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7023.......1.4300........-16.00% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr..31.7550......27.7500........-12.61% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1210.70.......842.00........-30.45% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....104.66.......114.40..........9.31% \par \par \uc2      ((Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3840;fax (65) 870-3787; email: \par \par \uc2  asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv9r0319k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal