\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA MARKETS-Stocks sink,  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  calm post-G7. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 985 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 1999\par 10:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 27 (Reuters) - Asian stocks remained prone \par \par \uc2  to jitters about U.S. asset markets on Monday while regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained ground after the Group of Seven meeting failed \par \par \uc2  to come up with measures to rein in the rising yen. \par \par \uc2      DOLLAR/YEN SPLUTTERS, REGIONALS HOLD FIRM \par \par \uc2      Analysts found little that was new in the G7 communique, \par \par \uc2  which said the group shared Japan's concern about the impact of \par \par \uc2  the rising yen and welcomed efforts by Tokyo to conduct its \par \par \uc2  policies accordingly. \par \par \uc2      Speculation the Bank of Japan might take credit easing steps \par \par \uc2  to counter the yen's appreciation and pave the way for \par \par \uc2  coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  initially boosted the dollar to 106 \par \par \uc2  yen. \par \par \uc2      But its rally was short-lived and analysts said the dollar's \par \par \uc2  downtrend remained intact. \par \par \uc2      "The bearish trend of dollar/yen shows no sign of reversal. \par \par \uc2  We would recommend re-instating short positions at 105.90 yen \par \par \uc2  with a stop above the 21-day moving average at 107.50," said \par \par \uc2  Chin Loo Thio, strategist at Paribas. \par \par \uc2  Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were resilient to the yen's early falls \par \par \uc2  as players took profit on long dollar positions after last \par \par \uc2  week's big losses in the baht, peso and rupiah. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN STOCKS SINK BUT DAMAGE CONTAINED - FOR NOW \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's stock market featured prominently as trade resumed \par \par \uc2  after a four-day break following last week's massive earthquake. \par \par \uc2      The weighted index gapped sharply lower at the open with \par \par \uc2  chipmakers predictably bearing the brunt of the decline. \par \par \uc2      But the damage was contained by buying in the construction \par \par \uc2  and cement sectors, and by a newly narrowed volatility limit \par \par \uc2  which left trade in about 85 percent of listed companies \par \par \uc2  suspended for the day after the first half-hour. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry on Sunday ordered the narrowing of \par \par \uc2  volatility limits in its stock and futures markets to 3.5 \par \par \uc2  percent from seven percent to avoid panic-selling. The new limit \par \par \uc2  remains in place until October 8. \par \par \uc2  But Taipei brokers said the market was set to head much \par \par \uc2  lower, with sell orders, mainly from local retail investors, \par \par \uc2  piling up after the suspension of trade. \par \par \uc2      Technically, the weighted index could soon test support just \par \par \uc2  below the 7,700 level to fill a gap created on August 16. \par \par \uc2      Taiwan stock futures traded on SIMEX in Singapore also made \par \par \uc2  hefty losses, with the key September contract gapping down \par \par \uc2  sharply after a three-day suspension. \par \par \uc2      The falls were somewhat cushioned by trading limits, though \par \par \uc2  these are not nearly as rigid as in Taiwan. \par \par \uc2      And dealers said the market could see some consolidation, as \par \par \uc2  the key September contract looks heavily oversold, with a 14-day \par \par \uc2  RSI reading of about 17. \par \par \uc2      THAI BAHT PERKS UP, BUT PROSPECTS POOR \par \par \uc2      The Thai baht firmed back to the right side of 41 per dollar \par \par \uc2  as players booked profit on the dollar's rise to 13-month highs \par \par \uc2  last week. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said there were also rumours that the Bank of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in swap markets late on Friday and this \par \par \uc2  spurred players to reduce their long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said last Thursday that it was keeping a \par \par \uc2  close watch on the baht, but had found no evidence of a \par \par \uc2  speculative attack and did not plan to act on its weakness. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said the baht's rebound on Monday was likely to be \par \par \uc2  short-lived. \par \par \uc2      "We're not looking for any sudden turnaround in the baht \par \par \uc2  anytime soon. We're still looking for a target of 43, but that \par \par \uc2  is a six-month view," said Kate O'Donoghue, regional economist \par \par \uc2  at Barclays Capital. \par \par \uc2  She said any upside was likely to be limited by worries \par \par \uc2  about Thailand's persistently high level of non-performing \par \par \uc2  loans, the slow pace of bank restructuring and a deflationary \par \par \uc2  environment. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday that total NPLs of Thai \par \par \uc2  banks amounted to 46.12 percent of total credits at end-July \par \par \uc2  against 46.48 percent a month earlier. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day MON 27 0831GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8350.00......8640.00.........3.47% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........40.74........41.17.........1.06% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........40.67........40.88.........0.52% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7026.......1.7072.