\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht down sharply on corporate dollar demand. \b0\par\par\uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 1999\par 13:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  1110 GMT - Thai baht down sharply against the dollar in late trade on strong corporate demand for the U.S \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * Baht 41.26/41.33 per dlr late vs 40.53/40.58 early Thursday \par \par \uc2  * Baht 43.0878/43.1816 per euro vs 42.3376/42.4305 \par \par \uc2  * Y 104.08/104.13 per dlr vs 103.82/103.87 \par \par \uc2  * Overnight interbank rate 1.125-1.25 pct \par \par \uc2  * One-month forward swap discounts at -9.50/-8.50 satangs onshore; 0.00/2.00 satangs offshore \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-day repurchase rate 0.6875. \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Sept 23 (Reuters) - The baht lost almost 70 satangs against the dollar on Thursday due to huge demand for the U.S \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Thai corporates for debt settlements. \par \par \uc2  The baht hit at a day-low of 41.30 to the dollar at 1118 GMT in the London market, its lowest level since hitting 41.80 on August 31 last year. \par \par \uc2  "The baht was surrounded by piles of sell orders," said a trader at a major European bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the unit could test support around 41.50 to 41.65 tonight in U.S and European trading time. \par \par \uc2  "I don't want to imagine where it will be after it breaks through that level. But many are looking at some where around 42.00," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they saw a few profit-taking moves in afternoon trade. \par \par \uc2  "But that's not strong enough to push up the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Many players are beting on a much weaker baht," said another dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  He forecast that the baht would hit 41.80 overnight, a level it last hit on August 31, last year. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand said earlier on Thursday the baht's recent weakness against the dollar was due to limited dollar supply in the money market. \par \par \uc2  Tasana Rachatapo, director of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's banking department, told reporters exporters had been holding on to dollars due to low premiums in the forward swap market. \par \par \uc2  The strengthened yen had also encouraged Thai concerns that had borrowed in yen to rush to settle Japanese debts. \par \par \uc2  Investors also unwound the baht because of low Thai interest rates, she said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they had not detected any market-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Kitti Patpongpibul told reporters earlier on Thursday the authorities were keeping a close watch on the baht but found no evidence of any speculative attack on the unit. \par \par \uc2  He said the bank did not plan to act at the moment. \par \par \uc2  ((Ekarin Petsiri, Bangkok Newsroom +66-2 637 5500 ext 417 \par \par \uc2  email:bangkok.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv9n03dp7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
