\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht breaks below 40.80 support on dlr demand. \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 1999\par 09:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Sept 23 (Reuters) - The baht broke through significant support at 40.80 to the dollar in Thursday afternoon trade on high demand for the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the baht to test its next support of 41.00 later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The baht hit 40.90, its lowest level since September 9 last year, when it traded at 41.00 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The baht is being oversold against the dollar by local corporates with foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debts," said a dealer at a major local bank. "The unit will remain on the downside throughout afternoon trade." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand said on Thursday the baht's recent weakness against the dollar was due to limited dollar supply in the money market. \par \par \uc2  Tasana Rachatapo, director of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's banking department, told reporters exporters had been holding on to dollars due to low premiums in the forward swap market. \par \par \uc2  The strengthened yen had also encouraged Thai concerns that had borrowed in yen to rush to settle Japanese debts. \par \par \uc2  Investors also unwound the baht because of low Thai interest rates, she said. \par \par \uc2  Tasana said investors had previously borrowed in yen and deposited the loans at Thai banks, which used to offer far higher rates than in Japan. \par \par \uc2  "The (interest rate) gap has recently been considerably narrower," she said. \par \par \uc2  Fixed deposit rates at Thai banks have fallen to about 4.00 to 4.75 percent from a peak of more than 10 percent in the middle of last year. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they did not see any market-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Kitti Patpongpibul told reporters earlier on Thursday the authority was keeping a close watch on the baht but found no evidence of any speculative attack on the unit. He said the bank did not plan to act at the moment. \par \par \uc2  ((Ekarin Petsiri in Bangkok Newsroom +66-2 637-5500 ext 417 \par \par \uc2  e-mail:bangkok.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv9n03b63\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
