\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Opens Low -3: Stable Midmorning THB40.05-.10 \b0\par\par\uc2 218 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 1999\par 06:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The dollar stabilized in morning trade in a narrow range of THB40.05-.10, just above the previous Asian close. \par \par \uc2  At 0339 GMT, the dollar was at THB40.055. \par \par \uc2  Dealers confirmed Friday that they shared the perception of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that there was no unusual trading activity behind recent weakness in the baht. \par \par \uc2  Some expect the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar moves higher, toward a range of THB40.25-.50. \par \par \uc2  But another move up isn't expected in the short term. Short-term support for the dollar is at THB40 or THB39.90. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to damp volatility or deter speculative activity, not to fight market trends. \par \par \uc2  Only a very few analysts predict further weakness for the baht, however, and most see the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthening from current levels. \par \par \uc2  Some of the baht bulls have admitted that investment inflows may slow for the rest of the year until the possibility of any Y2K risk is out of the way. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's strong trade surplus and direct investment inflows are expected to outweigh capital outflows for debt repayment. \par \par \uc2  -By Thomas Fox; 662-266-0744; tfox@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-09-99 \par \par \uc2  0408GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9h06tpk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich