\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht/THB40 -3: Last Local Trade At THB40.05/Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 459 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1999\par 12:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  At 0955 GMT, DBS Thai Danu Bank executed its last trade of the day at THB40.05 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Satian Tantanasarit, a senior vice president in the bank's treasury department, said he expects the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in Asian trade Friday if the dollar climbs to a range of THB40.25 to THB40.50. \par \par \uc2  "They should if they want to stem the baht's fall," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to damp volatility, not to fight market trends. The government said it has neither a strong-baht nor weak-baht policy, as it must balance the interests of debtors who benefit from the former against the those of exporters who prefer the latter. \par \par \uc2  Satian added that he expects profit-taking soon, however, on long-dollar positions set up about eight-to-nine weeks ago. The dollar has been climbing since June, when it hit this year's low of THB36.51. \par \par \uc2  When the profit-taking comes, whether Friday or next week, Satian said he doesn't expect investors to start building up new long-dollar positions until the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  corrects to around THB39.50. \par \par \uc2  The baht, the Philippine peso, and to a lesser extent, the Singapore dollar, have recently followed the Indonesian rupiah lower on contagion from violence in East Timor. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted that despite stability in the rupiah Thursday, sentiment was very negative, with the president and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  implicated in a banking scandal, and a high probability of complications upon entry as early as this weekend of a U.N. peacekeeping force into Timor. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, foreign investors in the Thai stock market have been net sellers more often than net buyers recently, as investors appear to be locking in gains. The dealer said these investors might be reluctant to reenter the market for the remainder of the year due to the Y2K risk, he said. \par \par \uc2  The outlook for the Thai stock market is still positive, despite a drop of 2% Thursday in the composite SET index to 429.89 points, due to increasing signs of renewed growth in the Thai economy after two years of recession. \par \par \uc2  Analysts also believe that Thailand's strong trade surplus and direct investment inflows will be sufficient to balance outflows to pay down foreign debts. \par \par \uc2  The commerce ministry said Thursday that August exports were up 14.7% on year, while exports in the first eight months rose 3.4% on year. Official August data is due for release by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the end of September. \par \par \uc2  -By Thomas Fox; 662-266-0744; tfox@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 16-09-99 \par \par \uc2  1034GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9g06tkz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
