\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht breaks key 40/dlr level late. \b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1999\par 12:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0947 GMT - Thai baht\tab   breaks the key 40/dlr level late on heavy selling of the unit offshore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Baht 40.00/40.05 per dlr late vs 39.40/39.45 early\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  * Y 104.14/104.24 vs dlr against 105.03/105.08 \par \par \uc2  * Overnight interbank rate at 1.25-1.75 pct \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-day repurchase rate 0.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Sept 16 (Reuters) - The baht broke through key psychological support at 40 baht to the dollar on steady sales of the unit offshore and the Thai government's reiteration it saw no need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  At 1020 GMT, the baht tumbled further to 40.05 to 40.10 to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , its lowest level since September 23 last year. \par \par \uc2  The sharp loss also came after a meeting between Japan's Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa and Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami on the yen's recent sharp rise resulted in little of substance. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect the Bank of Japan to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market as a strong yen would hamper the pace of recovery of Asia's largest economy, and subsequently that of other Asian nations. \par \par \uc2  "When the baht surged this morning, it was not in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which were weak. There was not any attack on the baht," said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  Deputy Finance Minister Pisit Leeahtam said on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 currenct\b0 \highlight\uc2  baht level was "OK" and the government had no plan to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The baht should be dictated by market forces. The current level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is OK. There is no irregular movement so far," he told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also poured more cold water on any kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Assistant Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor, Chetthavee Charoenpitaks said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline was normal and there was no reason to panic. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht would likely stay around 40.00 to 40.10 baht and was unlikely to be weaker as "there will be profit taking after that," said another dealer at a foreign bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  ((Ekarin Petsiri in Bangkok Newsroom +662 637-5500 ext 417 \par \par \uc2  e-mail:bangkok.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9g00kpp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
