\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA MARKETS - Ease on yen wobbles, U.S. rate fears. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Tamora Vidaillet \par \uc2 790 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 1999\par 11:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 16 (Reuters) - Jitters over possible \par \par \uc2  Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pressured the yen and other regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, as Asian stock markets bowed to fears \par \par \uc2  of another U.S. interest hike. \par \par \uc2      News that Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa was \par \par \uc2  meeting Bank of Japan governor Masaru Hayami to discuss \par \par \uc2  monetary policy stoked fears \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be imminent, \par \par \uc2  propping the dollar up briefly against the yen. \par \par \uc2      Chin Loo Thio, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Paribas, said in a \par \par \uc2  daily report the dollar was technically unlikely to find a \par \par \uc2  bottom until September 29, the end of the first half of Japan's \par \par \uc2  fiscal year. \par \par \uc2      "Once September is over, the need for yen purchases may \par \par \uc2  decline as both Japanese exporters and investors complete their \par \par \uc2  hedges," she said. \par \par \uc2      RUPIAH SLIPS BACK BEYOND 8,000 \par \par \uc2      The rupiah eased to the wrong side of the 8,000 per dollar \par \par \uc2  level as players maintained their wait-and-see approach to the \par \par \uc2  smouldering Bank Bali scandal and plans to move a U.N. peace \par \par \uc2  keeping force to East Timor. \par \par \uc2      Some dealers in Jakarta said fears the U.N.'s presence \par \par \uc2  could heighten animosity in the bloodied territory were \par \par \uc2  overwhelming relief over the impending arrival of foreign \par \par \uc2  troops. \par \par \uc2      Sentiment was also weak due to comments by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  that an audit into the Bank Bali scandal had been unfair and \par \par \uc2  that loan delays by the World Bank and the IMF could harm the \par \par \uc2  economy. \par \par \uc2      And \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Syahril Sabirin warned that Bank \par \par \uc2  Indonesia could take legal action against \par \par \uc2  PricewaterhouseCoopers, which conducted the audit. \par \par \uc2      "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is underpinned by quite tight monetary policy \par \par \uc2  in Indonesia but politically, the threat is still great," said \par \par \uc2  Kate O'Donoghue, regional economist at Barclays Capital Asia. \par \par \uc2      "Volatility will be on the cards for quite some time," she \par \par \uc2  told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2      PESO RISK RETURN SEEN WORTHY DESPITE DEFICIT \par \par \uc2      The peso was placed under added pressures by prospects of a \par \par \uc2  widening budget deficit one day after the IMF agreed to a 10 \par \par \uc2  billion peso increase to this year's fiscal shortfall. \par \par \uc2  Socio-economic planning secretary Felipe Medalla said next \par \par \uc2  year's deficit was also likely to overshoot the 40 billion peso \par \par \uc2  target by about 10 billion pesos. \par \par \uc2  But analysts remained upbeat on the Philippines. \par \par \uc2  "The Philippines' chronic fiscal deficit has made them \par \par \uc2  develop a healthy T-bill market so we are still quite bullish \par \par \uc2  on the peso. The economy is suffering more from cyclical \par \par \uc2  problems than from structural ones," Barclays Capital's \par \par \uc2  O'Donoghue said. \par \par \uc2      "We see the peso offering value and we would certainly be \par \par \uc2  looking to buy it at these levels," she said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 THAILAND\b0 \highlight\uc2  RULES OUT \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  ON BAHT \par \par \uc2      The baht hovered near its year lows, pressured as the yen \par \par \uc2  came off its high, but the government said it had no plans to \par \par \uc2  step in. \par \par \uc2      Thai Deputy Finance Minister Pisit Leeahtam said current \par \par \uc2  baht levels were okay and the government had no plans to \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      "The baht should be dictated by market forces. The current \par \par \uc2  level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is okay. There is no irregular movement \par \par \uc2  so far," he told reporters in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2      KOSPI SLIDES AMID LIQUIDITY FEARS \par \par \uc2      Korean stocks slid more than three percent partly due to an \par \par \uc2  uptick in domestic interest rates triggered by liquidity fears. \par \par \uc2      The benchmark three-year Treasury bond yield crossed the \par \par \uc2  9.5 percent mark amid fears Daewoo's financial troubles could \par \par \uc2  spark a run on investment companies in November, when more \par \par \uc2  redemptions of beneficiary certificates are to be allowed. \par \par \uc2      Investment trusts hold 75 percent of the 30.75 trillion won \par \par \uc2  ($25.8 billion) in Daewoo's bonds and commercial papers. \par \par \uc2      Some analysts said the direction of the KOSPI -- which has \par \par \uc2  yielded dollar-based year-to-date returns of over 88 percent -- \par \par \uc2  depends on future government handling of Daewoo's problems. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day THU 16 0911GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah.......8120.00......8000.00......-1.48% \par \par \uc2   Baht.........39.93....... 39.40........-1.33% \par \par \uc2   Peso.........40.15........39.94........-0.52% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6917.......1.6880.......-0.22% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...31.705.......31.710........0.02% \par \par \uc2   Korean won...1198.50......1192.60......-0.49% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....103.95.......104.19........0.23% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest........July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah.......8120.00......2432.00.......-70.05% \par \par \uc2   Baht.........39.92........25.90.........-35.12% \par \par \uc2   Peso.........40.15........26.50.........-34.00% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6917.......1.4300........-15.47% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...31.7050......27.7500.......-12.47% \par \par \uc2   Korean won...1198.50......842.00........-29.75% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....103.95.......114.40.........10.05%. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9g00kkl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
