\par\par \b \uc2  Thai c.bank confirms no baht  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  recently. \b0\par\par\uc2 168 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 1999\par 10:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Sept 15 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it had not entered the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets recently to shore up the baht and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movement should be dictated by market forces. \par \par \uc2  Assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chetthavee Charoenpitaks told Reuters the recent fall in the value of the baht was temporary and the bank was closely watching the situation. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not done anything in the (\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) markets. We don't care much about specific baht levels - our concern is to ensure a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  Chetthavee said the baht's weakness was mainly due to the strength of the yen, which recently hit its highest level since May 1996. \par \par \uc2  The baht was traded at 39.40/39.50 to the dollar on Wednesday afternoon against 39.55/39.58 late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Bangkok Newsroom +66-2 637 5500 ext 418 \par \par \uc2  email:bangkok.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9f00ijb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
