\par\par \b \uc2  INTERVIEW/ \highlight22\uc2 Thailand \highlight\uc2 's Supachai-2:Ctrl Bk Hasn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By Tracy Withers \par \uc2 744 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 1999\par 01:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  AUCKLAND (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy prime minister and commerce minister, Supachai Panitchapdi, said he isn't worried by a recent fall in the baht, and believes it will eventually settle at an export-friendly level. \par \par \uc2  In an interview, Supachai also said year-on-year growth in the second quarter would be around 8% or 9%, well above the original target of 1% or 2%. Export growth in 1999 is now seen at 3.5%, from around 1% previously, he said. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the baht fell to an 11-month low as the dollar reached THB39.730. The dollar finished Asian trading Friday at THB39.465, down marginally from THB39.485 at the close Thursday. The weakness was linked to a slide in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in reaction to turmoil in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  Supachai told Dow Jones Newswires that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at all in recent days and said the government will let the baht "find a new level, hopefully a level that will be helpful to export promotion from Thailand. \par \par \uc2  "The only thing we have to cope with is a short-term fluctuation of fund flows because of the security concern in this part of the world," he said, referring to international concern over the violence in the Indonesian province of East Timor. \par \par \uc2  "This won't be with us forever. It will go away one of these days and we're back to normal business," he said. \par \par \uc2  Supachai noted that when the baht rose in June and July to around THB35 per dollar, there was fear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength was excessive. Now that it has fallen toward THB40, it shows that the baht is centering around a range of THB36 to THB38 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "If you look at the fundamentals you shouldn't be overly worried that there is a declining trend for the baht, or an upward trend," he said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the level of reserves near US$32 billion, monthly trade\par surpluses of US$500 million to US$900 million, and expected substantial\par capital inflows into shares and to purchase two banks marked for sale,\par were fundamentals supporting the outlook for the baht.\par -\par Says Need To Address Bad Loans\par -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts have also highlighted slow progress in restructuring\par nonperforming loans within the banking system as a factor behind the\par weak baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Supachai said the average level of nonperforming loans is around 46%\par to 47% of the total lending portfolio, but there are banks with higher\par levels just as there are those with lower levels.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We have to tackle those banks (with high levels)," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said some loans can be restructured, and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is\par working with commercial banks to agree on the definition of some loans,\par and this will lower the level of nonperforming loans. "They have to\par agree how to reschedule some of these loans," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However the final solution will be sales of some banks, and successful\par merger of other banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Supachai said Thailand's letter of intent to the International\par Monetary Fund has been delayed by the need for reassessment of economic\par data "which is much more positive" and which changes the "background\par against which we make our decisions."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said second quarter gross domestic product should grow 8% or 9%\par from original targets of 1% or 2%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai government said Friday that the letter of intent for the\par coming ninth quarter of the IMF's US$17.2 billion rescue program will be\par considered by the cabinet Sept. 21, and not Tuesday as previously\par indicated.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, Supachai said he has no concern with the emerging trend of\par free-trade arrangements between economies within APEC "if they serve the\par purpose of reducing tariffs and don't discriminate against third\par countries.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It might seem to be distracting from the original objective of APEC,\par but if the countries are pushing for more trade liberalization, and are\par not jeopardizing trade with third countries they should be supported and\par allowed," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said "more are being arranged, and will be arranged," noting that\par Thailand is considering arrangements with South Korea and China.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Supachai said the arrangements are consistent with his original\par proposal to have closer links between the Association of Southeast Asian\par Nations and the Closer Economic Relationship arrangement between\par Australia and New Zealand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Tracy Withers; tracy.withers@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 12-09-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2308GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv9c06p4d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
