\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht firms late on offshore dlr profit taking. \b0\par\par\uc2 425 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 September 1999\par 12:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0920 GMT - Thai baht\tab   firmer on offshore profit-taking and Japan's better-than-expected gross domestic product data\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Baht 39.45/39.55 per dlr late vs intraday low of 39.76 at midday and 39.60/39.65 early on Thursday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  * Baht 41.8249/41.9388 per euro vs 42.0037/42.0647 \par \par \uc2  * Y 109.10/109.20 per dlr vs 109.11/109.16 \par \par \uc2  * Overnight interbank rate at 1.25-2.00 pct \par \par \uc2  * One-month forward swap discounts quoted at -10.50/-9.50 satangs per dlr onshore; 3.00/5.00 satangs offshore \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-day repurchase rate 0.75 percent. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BANGKOK, Sept 9 (Reuters) - Thai baht\tab   rebounded slightly in late trade on Thursday as players offshore started to take profits in dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai unit, along with Singapore dollar and the rupiah, was also received a boost from the stronger yen, which rose on better than expected Japan GDP data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said concern that Japan may announce GDP contraction had triggered a fall in some regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the past two days.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 0920 GMT, the baht was quoted at 39.45/39.55 against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , from an intraday high of 39.76 around midday and 39.45/39.55 in early Asian trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The degree of volatility is considered high because of the constant profit-taking," said a dealer at a local bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We have heard that offshore selling of the dollar was very active because investors are not as worried about the situation as they were (on Wednesday)," the dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah, which was initially forecast to remain a pressure on the baht and other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , regained some lost ground on Thursday afternoon after the overbought dollar failed to decisively break resistance at 9,000 rupiah.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Jakarta said it had become clearer how the Indonesian government would handle the East Timor problem. Government officials had also given some positive comments on the situation, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Though the baht showed recovery in the afternoon trade, dealers said there was no Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to help the baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Prime Minister Chuan Leekpai said on Thursday the government has no plan to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Chuan said the baht's fall was temporary and the market would be left to decide the level of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Ekarin Petsiri +66-2 637 5500 ext 417\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par email:bangkok.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9900wgm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
