\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht weakens further on East Timor concerns. \b0\par\par\uc2 433 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 1999\par 05:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0225 GMT - Thai baht\tab   weaker due to investor concerns about the unsettled chaos in East Timor that has prompted sales of the rupiah and other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Baht 39.32/39.35 per dlr early vs 39.02/39.05 late Tuesday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  * Baht at lowest level since October 2 last year \par \par \uc2  * Baht 41.6553/41.7264 per euro vs 40.9006/40.9728 \par \par \uc2  * Y 111.01/111.06 vs 109.66/109.69 \par \par \uc2  * One-month forward swap discounts quoted at -10.50/-9.50 satangs per dlr onshore; 0.00/2.00 offshore \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-day repurchase rate 0.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Sept 8 (Reuters) - The baht plunged to its lowest level since October 2 last year as investors sold it along with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on concern over political unrest in East Timor. \par \par \uc2  Last October 2, the baht was traded at 39.40 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht, the Philippine peso and Singapore dollar, were dumped along with the Indonesian rupiah as investors wanted to minimise risk in holding South East Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Offshore players squared positions to cut losses from the rupiah. They also sold other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with higher liquidity," said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said any uptrend for the baht was still limited as foreign players were panicked about the situation in Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  "We expect the first resistance on the baht at 39.20 and the second at 38.90," he said. Support is seen at 39.40. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer at a foreign bank said he still did not see any sign of market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I hadn't heard of that, and I don't think they will. Market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  under present circumstancse would be wasteful defence," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda on Tuesday night said the government was not in favour of a strong baht because a firmer \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could affect the nation's exports. \par \par \uc2  "We will try to primarily keep the baht weaker in order to help exporters and as it could be a factor contributing to the (Thai) economic recovery," he told a social club gethering. \par \par \uc2  Tarrin's stance differs from that of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which said last Friday the baht had been undervalued and the real value should be about 33 baht to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  At 0300 GMT, the baht was firmer at 39.28 to 39.33 baht to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The unit hit its day low of 39.35 in early Asian trade. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv9801274\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
