\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand/Reserves-3:Reserves Up Despite Rumored Dlr Sales \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1999\par 12:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  A Bank of Thailand official said its foreign reserves rose $300 million in U.S. dollar terms during the week ended Aug. 20 due to the appreciation of other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Japanese yen appreciated over the period to about Y112 to the dollar from around Y115. \par \par \uc2  The increase came as rumors circulated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars this week to cap the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at THB38.50, after it rose from THB36.50 two months earlier. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets only to prevent volatility, not to fight market trends. \par \par \uc2  It also has a policy of accumulating foreign reserves. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the sharp decrease in net claims on financial institutions in the week ended Aug. 20 was due to the injection of capital by the government into the state-run Krung Thai Bank PCL under its financial sector restructuring program. \par \par \uc2  Loans from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Financial Institutions Development Fund worth THB108 billion were converted into new shares in the bank. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said the injection of capital had no impact on the monetary base because the debt was transformed into equity. \par \par \uc2  The decrease in the monetary base was due to a decline in deposits of financial institutions at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and a normal decrease in cash held by the public in the middle of the month. \par \par \uc2  Net claims on the government decreased because the FIDF sold government bonds at auctions to financial institutions in the amount of THB9.3 billion. The government also recorded a cash surplus in the week. \par \par \uc2  -By Chanyaporn Chanjaroen; 662-266-0744; cchanjaroen@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 27-08-99 \par \par \uc2  1010GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8r06e4v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
