\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Dep Fin Min: Stable Baht, Reforms Helping Recovery \b0\par\par\uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1999\par 06:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--Thailand's Deputy Finance Minister Pisit Leeahtam said the Thai government is happy with the current level of the baht, and with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is working to keep a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to sustain a pattern of emerging growth. \par \par \uc2  Pisit was commenting at the fringes of an Asia Pacific Economic Cooperation forum deputy finance officials meeting in Wellington Friday. \par \par \uc2  He told Dow Jones Newswires that the baht has now been stable for around 16 months, and that the government is comfortable with the THB36 to THB38 levels it has been trading in. \par \par \uc2  The combination of a strong yen and factors that tend to have the opposite effect - such as the prospect of a weakening in the yuan and tensions between China and Taiwan - have caused volatility recently in many Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Pisit said \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  is willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the baht from reacting violently to other influential \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a role to play in definitely trying to quell the rapid movements of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but they must not put rigidity into the exchange system," Pisit said. \par \par \uc2  "They must not try to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a certain price (so) must allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move along with fundamentals," he said. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand has stated that it bought dollars to damp volatility and build foreign reserves as the baht tended to strengthen in the second quarter. Since then, it reportedly sold dollars to cap the its rise at THB38.50. \par \par \uc2  Pisit said countries like Thailand shouldn't be complacent regarding further economic shocks. The government is working to build strong foundations through corporate governance, transparency in financial systems and organizations, and risk management, he said. \par \par \uc2  "All these have to be new disciplines for the private sector. In the past decade they have been a bit too complacent and lax in terms of financial discipline. They borrowed too much, they had too much \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure," Pisit said. \par \par \uc2  "For them to survive and grow in the next decade, they have to build a strong foundation and discipline, and also creating a lot more corporate etiquette," he added. \par \par \uc2  He said once this new structure has been created, the growth momentum now being experienced should be sustainable. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 27-08-99 \par \par \uc2  0405GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv8r06d2q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
