\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Thailand \highlight\uc2  reiterates won't  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to curb baht. \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 1999\par 06:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, June 29 (Reuters) - Thai deputy finance minister, Pisit Leeatham, reiterated on Tuesday the government would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the baht's recent gains and would leave the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to find its own market level. \par \par \uc2  He told reporters: "The authorities would be unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I think it (the baht) is now suitable and should be left to find its own level." \par \par \uc2  The minister said Thai exports had increased at a satisfactory pace in recent months despite concerns at the commerce ministry that the sector had not been helped by a stronger baht. \par \par \uc2  Thai May exports rose an estimated 8.4 percent year-on-year in dollar terms, the second monthly growth posted after a contraction of 6.8 percent for the whole of 1998. \par \par \uc2  The baht firmed to a five-month high of about 36.55 to the dollar last week and has since stayed in the 36.65-36.85 range compared with 37.00-38.00 in the past four months. \par \par \uc2  Pisit's comments echoed those of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul who said on Monday that the baht was not too strong. \par \par \uc2  The minister said a one to two baht appreciation of the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not make any big impact on export performance. \par \par \uc2  "We have seen the baht falling to 36-37 from 25-26 (to the dollar). Isn't that enough (for helping exports)?", he said, referring to the baht's pre-devaluation level before July 1997. \par \par \uc2  ((Vithoon Amorn, Bangkok newsroom (662)-6375500 ext 412 \par \par \uc2  e-mail: bangkok.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6t05gy1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
