\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA MARKETS - Relaxed about likely Fed move. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 946 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 1999\par 10:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, June 29 (Reuters) - Asian markets held their \par \par \uc2  ground on Tuesday as the yen meandered in familiar ranges and \par \par \uc2  investors took a more relaxed view of a widely expected U.S. \par \par \uc2  rate hike. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said a U.S. tightening was unlikely to spark fears \par \par \uc2  of similar moves in Asia, where most central banks are still \par \par \uc2  trying to jump-start bank lending in the wake of the crisis. \par \par \uc2      "The central banks' key policy focus at the moment is to \par \par \uc2  maintain monetary policy which provides for growth rather than \par \par \uc2  stable exchange rate targets," said John Woods, head of \par \par \uc2  research at HSBC Markets in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2      "Whatever the Fed does, at this juncture, that particular \par \par \uc2  policy isn't going to be upset," Woods told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2      KOREAN OUTPUT SURGES, MARKETS UNIMPRESSED \par \par \uc2      South Korea had yet more proof that its economy is out of \par \par \uc2  the woods. \par \par \uc2      Industrial output jumped 21.8 percent in May, its biggest \par \par \uc2  year-on-year rise in more than a decade. \par \par \uc2      But the base effect was quite sharp, given last May's \par \par \uc2  eleven percent contraction in output. \par \par \uc2      The current account surplus also continued to shrink in \par \par \uc2  May, with close to a 50 percent year-on-year fall, reflecting a \par \par \uc2  growing hunger for imports as domestic demand recovers. \par \par \uc2      But the strong numbers had little impact on Korean markets, \par \par \uc2  as investors opted to take profit on the KOSPI's surge Monday. \par \par \uc2      The won also failed to make headway in a market wary of \par \par \uc2  further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but heavy with dollars from exporter \par \par \uc2  deals. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars sporadically, \par \par \uc2  signalling its unease with a strengthening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after \par \par \uc2  Monday's purchases of an estimated $100-$150 million. \par \par \uc2      TAIWAN SHARES SHINE, BUT CHART OUTLOOK UNCERTAIN \par \par \uc2      Taiwan shares had a stellar session, thanks to Wall \par \par \uc2  Street's overnight gains and a near-two percent rise in the \par \par \uc2  tech-heavy U.S. Nasdaq. \par \par \uc2      Taiwan's weighted index has broken above important \par \par \uc2  technical resistance at 8,410 which marks a 61.8 percent \par \par \uc2  retracement of the pre-crisis high to the low earlier this \par \par \uc2  year. \par \par \uc2      But on the short-term charts, the picture is less clear, \par \par \uc2  with a couple of gaps opening up in the past few sessions. \par \par \uc2      If the market drops sharply for any reason, it could still \par \par \uc2  pull back to fill an exhaustion gap around the 8,060 level, \par \par \uc2  which opened on June 17. \par \par \uc2      And if that downmove opens up a downside breakaway gap, it \par \par \uc2  will have very bearish implications for the near-term trend. \par \par \uc2      But for the time being, foreign flows to the stock market \par \par \uc2  were keeping the Taiwan dollar on firm footing, though dealers \par \par \uc2  were wary of pushing it too far. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Perng Fai-nan said on Monday the bank \par \par \uc2  only defends the Taiwan dollar when "irregular or seasonal \par \par \uc2  factors" emerge, and its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  do not defy economic \par \par \uc2  fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  BAHT STEADY DESPITE C.BANK ASSURANCES \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht was dragging its feet despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's insistance that it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to influence the \par \par \uc2  exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul said the \par \par \uc2  baht's current rate at around 36.60-36.80 per dollar was backed \par \par \uc2  by sound fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  His view was echoed by the finance ministry. But the \par \par \uc2  market's likely to be less than convinced after Deputy Prime \par \par \uc2  Minister Supachai Panitchpakdi said last week the baht's \par \par \uc2  strength could hurt exports if its rallies were not checked. \par \par \uc2  Thai stocks bucked the generally firmer trend, with bank \par \par \uc2  shares leading the decline after news that a proposed takeover \par \par \uc2  of ailing Nakornthon Bank Plc by Britain's Standard Chartered \par \par \uc2  Bank had been called off. \par \par \uc2      The BOT said it instead planned to put Nakorthon up for \par \par \uc2  auction. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day TUE 29 0813GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000..........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......6640.00......6620.00.........-0.30% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.88........36.85.........-0.08% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........37.92........37.94..........0.05% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7040.......1.7033.........-0.04% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.275.......32.350..........0.23% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1157.00......1156.00.........-0.09% \par \par \uc2   Japan y