\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Asia: Thai Econ Recovery May Reverse Strong Baht \b0\par\par\uc2  By Thomas Fox \par \uc2 1,094 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 1999\par 07:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--While the Thai baht's rally looks likely to go unchecked for a few more months, a climb to THB35 to the dollar could force the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  into a head-to-head battle with the market, amid concern about the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the country's exports. \par \par \uc2  The baht will continue climbing as funds roll in ahead of an economic recovery expected to gather steam later this year, but most analysts see the dollar regaining ground to between THB36 and THB38 by year-end. \par \par \uc2  Authorities have said they find the current range of THB36.50 to THB37 to the dollar acceptable. But Prime Minister Chuan Leekpai and his Deputy Premier Supachai Panitchpakdi expressed concern last week that if the baht gets any stronger, it will choke off a recovery in export growth that just began in April, after 13 consecutive months of year-on-year contraction. \par \par \uc2  "A stronger baht isn't necessarily good for the recovery," said Satian Tantanasarit, senior vice president of DBS Thai Danu Bank PCL. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand is counting on export growth of 2.1% this year, to help meet a 1999 gross domestic product growth forecast of 1%, after two years of recession. \par \par \uc2  Rising capital inflows are paying no heed to the government's targets, however, and will eventually have their way. \par \par \uc2  "It's just a matter of time before we see a stronger baht," said Satian. \par \par \uc2  That was evident last Tuesday, when confirmation by an official that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to forswear \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against market trends prompted \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  players to sell down the dollar by THB0.30 from the previous day's close to finish at THB36.58. \par \par \uc2  A rising baht won't go unchecked: the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acts to damp volatility and accumulate foreign reserves by placing anonymous orders through agents in various markets. \par \par \uc2  But since its failed defense of the baht prior to the July 2, 1997, float of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has never drawn any lines in the sand and dared investors to step over them. \par \par \uc2  Supachai doesn't have direct authority in the matter, but he, for one, wants to draw that line now. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    THB35 May Force \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  To Drastic Action\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If we let the baht rise to THB35, it will be unbearable. It will hurt\par the economy," said Supachai, who is also commerce minister and head of\par the government's export promotion committee.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rob Collins, executive vice president of Paribas Asia Equity, agrees\par that THB35 is a critical level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think if it was to strengthen to THB35, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would be\par forced to take serious action," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Satian thinks so, too. He predicts the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will first step in\par at THB36.50, and then force investors who are pushing the baht higher to\par climb over the bank at every step.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think they will come into the market every five or 10 satang," he\par said, adding it will take more than just a few weeks to reach THB35 (1\par satang=THB0.01).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Supachai is counting on that delay, in the hope that factors will\par change and ease market pressure on the baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I hope that its strength will be just for a short period of time," he\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par According to some analysts, he has reason to be optimistic.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As the economy picks up, Thailand's trade surplus should narrow. A\par recovery in domestic demand would lead to higher imports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, Thai companies might step up repayment of foreign debt.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If the economy picks up and banks begin to lend again, all\par non-exporting companies will want to switch back into baht debt,"\par Paribas' Collins said. A weakening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  "would almost be a sign of\par recovery."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par An analyst at a European house in Bangkok, however, discounts the\par significance of debt repayments in capital outflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Domestic refinancing of foreign loans can't happen unless banks resume\par new lending, but institutions are reluctant to risk new lending amid a\par shortage of credit-worthy clients, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Armed with new legal and regulatory frameworks and facing steep\par increases in loan-loss reserve requirements every six months between now\par and end-2000, major banks are expected to step up workouts of\par non-performing loans, which account for 47% of outstanding credit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But resulting outflows won't be as big as expected, the European house\par analyst said. "In most restructurings, the money isn't repaid - it's\par swapped for equity or assets, or principal repayments are delayed."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Private-sector foreign debt has already fallen to about $50 billion\par from $67 billion last year, he added. "A lot of debts have already been\par paid down."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Foreign Investment Will Rise\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Arguing for the stronger side of the baht consensus range, around\par THB36 to THB36.50 against the dollar by year-end, the analyst said trade\par and current account surpluses will narrow, but on the other hand,\par private investment inflows will tend to pick up.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Aside from hot money flowing into Thai stocks, longer-term foreign\par direct investment will also increase in a recovery, offsetting a\par narrowing of the current account and then some, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We are not talking about investment in new capacity, but in existing\par capacity. There is a lot of talking going on, but when prices start to\par rise in a recovery, you will see a lot more deals" with new foreign\par partners, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At the bottom line, the European house analyst's view doesn't differ\par so much from that of Paribas' Collins.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Last month, Paribas lowered its year-end baht forecast to THB37 from\par THB40 to the dollar, in light of the recent influx of funds. Merrill\par Lynch & Co. is holding out at THB38, also recently revised down from\par THB40.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Robert McMillen, joint managing director at Seamico Securities PCL,\par said the dollar could end the year anywhere between THB35 and THB40,\par given Thailand's vulnerability to economic trends in the world's\par developed countries, which are its major export markets and creditors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But money is going to flow into Asia because it won't be profitable to\par keep it elsewhere, he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Global fund managers believe there is a good chance that U.S. stocks\par are headed for a major correction and the Euro is on the brink of a\par nose-dive. In Asia, Thailand and South Korea would be among the main\par beneficiaries, McMillen said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Thomas Fox; 662-266-0744; tfox@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 28-06-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0530GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4258 5095 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6s04v5v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
