\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals mixed, won remains firm. \b0\par\par\uc2 536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 1999\par 03:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0115 GMT - Regionals were mixed in narrow range, while \par \par \uc2  dollar-yen failed to move in decisive direction as it was \par \par \uc2  caught in a tug-of-war between concerns about U.S. asset \par \par \uc2  markets and the possibility of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \par \par \uc2  the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2      *** \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  earned an upgrade from rating agency Fitch \par \par \uc2  IBCA. The announcement came on Thursday after the prime \par \par \uc2  minister gave parliament better-than-expected GDP figures. \par \par \uc2      Fitch IBCA said it had raised Thailand's credit rating to \par \par \uc2  investment grade due to a marked improvement in the country's \par \par \uc2  external debt and liquidity situation. \par \par \uc2      Thailand's long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating was raised to \par \par \uc2  BBB minus from BB plus. Its short-term rating was raised to F3 \par \par \uc2  from B, it said. \par \par \uc2      *** South Korea had also won the approval of Fitch IBCA on \par \par \uc2  Thursday, and positive sentiment there has kept the won firm. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said they expected the ratings upgrade would invite \par \par \uc2  more foreign funds into Korea. \par \par \uc2      But dealers said they would continue to watch for \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The commerce ministry said in \par \par \uc2  early trade that South Korea would try to keep won-dollar \par \par \uc2  movement from hurting exports. \par \par \uc2  The won was also supported by comments from IMF's Hubert \par \par \uc2  Neiss, who said Korea's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  market were to smooth the movement of the won, not to weaken \par \par \uc2  it. \par \par \uc2      *** Hubert Neiss, visiting Hong Kong on Thursday, also said \par \par \uc2  there was still more room for the rupiah to strengthen. \par \par \uc2      He said a stronger rupiah would not cause problems for \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's recovery. \par \par \uc2      "On the contrary, the confidence that is created by the \par \par \uc2  strengthening rupiah, and in turn the strengthening rupiah's \par \par \uc2  influence on confidence, are good for the recovery," Neiss \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  *** Malaysian Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad said the \par \par \uc2  economy was growing well but he would not revise the official \par \par \uc2  GDP forecast of one percent expansion for this year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor has said GDP growth could exceed \par \par \uc2  the original forecast, possibly expanding by up to three \par \par \uc2  percent this year. \par \par \uc2  "Many people predict that growth will be more than one \par \par \uc2  percent, but the government will maintain its conservative \par \par \uc2  estimate," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Change on the day FRI 25 0130GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......6750.00......6735.00........-0.22% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.65........36.68.........0.08% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........37.95........37.86........-0.24% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7025.......1.7000........-0.15% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.300..