\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Rises On Ctrl Bk Comments, Strong Exports \b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1999\par 13:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht ended up sharply against the dollar Tuesday, after a Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  assistant governor reiterated that it will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against market trends, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished Tuesday at 36.58 baht (THB) down from THB36.88 at the close of trading in Bangkok Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Kiettisak Meecharoen told reporters that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only occur if the baht moved too strongly. \par \par \uc2  He said the economy was showing signs of renewed strength, so the baht was naturally rising, as the baht had fallen when the economy was weak. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market took this as a nod of acquiesence to a further strengthening of the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is expected to trade between THB36.50 and THB36.70 in the near term. \par \par \uc2  The baht is supported by renewed strength in exports, with 8.4% year-on-year growth reported from preliminary figures in May, and continued equity and direct investment inflows. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand set its reference rate at THB36.928 Tuesday, compared with THB36.870 Monday. The rate is a weighted average of rates charged by Thai commercial banks the previous trading day and serves as a benchmark for domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. \par \par \uc2  Swap and forward premiums dropped even lower Tuesday, compared with levels late Monday. Swap rates would rise in line with demand if the market believed the baht was going to depreciate. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Swap rates were as follows, in satang (THB1=100 satang):\par        Tuesday      Monday        Friday       Thursday\par 1-mo   -6.0/-3.0    -5.0/-4.0     -2.0/-1.0    -1.0\par 2-mo   -7.0/-5.0    -4.0/-2.5     -1.5/-0.5     0.5/1.5\par 3-mo   -8.0/-5.5    -4.0/-3.0     -2.0          1.0/2.5\par 6-mo   -8.0/-6.0       2.0         2.0/6.0      7.0/9.0\par 1-yr   -3.0/-2.0     5.0/10.0    15.0/20.0     22.0/25.0\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Thomas Fox; 662 266 0744; tfox@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 22-06-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1111GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6m04tgo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
