\par\par \b \uc2  Thai  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says won't restrain baht. \b0\par\par\uc2 154 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1999\par 10:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, June 22 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to restrain the baht and added that the current strength of baht would not hurt Thai exports. \par \par \uc2  Assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Kiatisak Meechareon told reporters the baht had strengthened due to growing confidence on the part of foreign investors in the positive outlook for a Thai economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "We will not do anything (to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets). The baht is changing only gradually against the dollar. We do not see any major volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Kiatisak said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht firmed after the official's comments, rising to around 36.67/36.70 to the dollar from 36.83/36.88 earlier on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Bangkok Newsroom +662 637-5500 ext 418 \par \par \uc2  e-mail:bangkok.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6m05x10\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
