\par\par \b \uc2  Thai  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  sees baht strength as temporary. \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 1999\par 14:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, May 10 (Reuters) - The governor of the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Chatu Mongol Sonakul, said on Monday the baht was being pushed up by flows of capital into Thailand and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength was likely to be temporary. \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol said he was not concerned by the baht's recent strength because the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to be adjusted by market mechanisms once it became too strong. \par \par \uc2  He said the recent inflows were mostly of capital invested in the stock market and not for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Thailand is not concerned about this because the baht is under the 'managed float system'," he said. \par \par \uc2  "When there are a lot of inflows coming in, it will strenthen temporarily. Once it becomes strong to the point that it is not attractive for investment, it will be adjusted by the market mechanism," he told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Under Thailand's "managed float system", the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows the baht to float freely but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  occasionally to try to iron out excess volatility. It does not seek to influence the overall direction of the baht. \par \par \uc2  The system was introduced in July 1997. \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw no need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market now as it believed in market mechanisms. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been in the market from time to time, not to influence the value of the baht but to buy dollars to meet its offshore swap obligations. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand said it had net forward \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales contracts of $3.9 billion to buy Thai baht as at April 30. \par \par \uc2  He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  normally buys dollar when the baht strengthens. \par \par \uc2  ((Bangkok newsroom +662 253-5000 ext 416, email:bangkok.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv5a01e1m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
