\par\par \b \uc2  Thai  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says won't move to support baht. \b0\par\par\uc2 261 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 1999\par 10:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Feb 22 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the baht. \par \par \uc2  Thai assistant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Kiettisak Meecharoen told reporters the baht had fallen recently due to external factors. \par \par \uc2  "We can not resist external factors. The baht weakness is in line with regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We have no plan to enter into the market to help shore up the baht," Kiettisak told reporters. \par \par \uc2  By 0920 GMT on Monday, the baht had fallen to around 37.70/37.75 to the dollar compared with 37.45/37.50 late on Friday after the Japanese yen fell under 122 yen per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Kiettisak said the yen fall was due to disappointment the G7 meeting over the weekend did not specifically address the recent yen weakness. \par \par \uc2  He said Thai economic fundamentals were unchanged but rising demand for the baht had helped boost short-term Thai interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-day repurchase rate closed at 5.875 on Monday morning, against 2.75 percent at the open. \par \par \uc2  Kiettisak said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was considering whether it would keep some of its forward contracts to buy Thai baht for cashflow management. \par \par \uc2  He expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's onshore swap forward commitments to decline to no more than $2.5 billion by the end of the year from $5.3 billion on February 12. \par \par \uc2  - Bangkok Newsroom (662) 253-5000 Ext 410 \par \par \uc2  - e-mail: rtrburo@ksc15.th.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2m0453a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
