\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Govt/Econ Bills-4: Govt To Maintain Most Current Policy \b0\par\par\uc2 394 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 1999\par 11:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Tarrin said the Dec. 2 letter was the only other document sent to the IMF, outside of the published letters of intent, in which the passage of the economic legislation is mentioned, contrary to the claims of the opposition in the censure debate last week. \par \par \uc2  He said the undisclosed side letters covered, for example, how the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when there was excess volatility between late 1997 and early 1998. The baht sank to a low of more than THB56 to the dollar in January 1998. \par \par \uc2  Some of the documents explained how the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market last year when commercial banks were competing for deposits by jacking up fixed-term deposit account interest rates and extending few new loans. \par \par \uc2  These practical measures could not be publicized as it would interfere with vital regulatory \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. \par \par \uc2  Tarrin said he could not say specifically when the seventh letter of intent, currently being drafted in consultation with the IMF, would be ready for cabinet approval. Talks with the IMF each quarter usually take about two weeks. The team arrived from Washington late last week. \par \par \uc2  The seventh letter of intent is likely to be shorter than previous letters, he said, because much of the policy measures outlined in the previous letter will be continued. \par \par \uc2  In the sixth letter, the government said it hoped to secure passage of the bankruptcy bill and related legislation by the end of the current parliamentary session March 22. \par \par \uc2  Observers think it's unlikely that the entire package of 11 economic reform bills will be passed in this session. \par \par \uc2  The government's bill to amend to the existing Bankruptcy Act has been passed by the House and is being scrutinized by a Senate committee. \par \par \uc2  If changes in committee alter the substance of the bill, and the changes are accepted by the full Senate, a joint House-Senate committee must work out a compromise for both houses to consider again. \par \par \uc2  The House has the power to enact the original version of the bill without Senate approval if no acceptable compromise can be agreed upon, but the government would rather win support for the controversial legislation. \par \par \uc2  -By Sinfah Tunsarawuth; 662-266-0744; stunsarawuth@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 02-02-99 \par \par \uc2  1011GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv2200vdx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
