\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals weaken on yuan fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 603 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 1999\par 10:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0900 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved lower on Monday \par \par \uc2  with the market alive with talk about the likelihood of a yuan \par \par \uc2  devaluation. \par \par \uc2      But the majority of analysts do not believe the Chinese \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be devalued or allowed to move lower in the \par \par \uc2  near-term. \par \par \uc2      Stock market falls stretched to more than five percent with \par \par \uc2  the fresh wave of selling was sparked by an article in the \par \par \uc2  official China Daily Business Weekly suggesting that a \par \par \uc2  devaluation or floating of the yuan may not be a bad thing. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the retreat reflected more and excuse to take \par \par \uc2  profits after the strong run up in regional stock markets over \par \par \uc2  the past few months, more than a genuine belief that the yuan \par \par \uc2  would be allowed to depreciate. \par \par \uc2  *** Malaysian Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad told foreign \par \par \uc2  investors that the government would review the ringgit's peg \par \par \uc2  against the U.S. dollar if it became a problem. \par \par \uc2  But Mahathir told a group of visiting fixed income managers \par \par \uc2  that Malaysia would not review the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, which was set \par \par \uc2  last September, in the immediate future. \par \par \uc2      *** The rupiah was the wrong side of 9,000 as it continues \par \par \uc2  its drift lower against the background of social unrest. \par \par \uc2      Worries about China also undermined the rupiah and dealers \par \par \uc2  said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support for the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      *** The Philippine peso was down quite sharply but there is \par \par \uc2  strong support at the 39 level. \par \par \uc2      *** The baht was also weaker with the market unsettled by \par \par \uc2  last week's bank results. \par \par \uc2      Thai banks announced record annual losses for 1998 last \par \par \uc2  week and analysts have ruled out hopes of a return to \par \par \uc2  profitability this year. \par \par \uc2      Fourteen Thai banks, including five already taken over by \par \par \uc2  the Thai government amid the country's economic crisis, \par \par \uc2  reported combined losses of $9 billion for last year. \par \par \uc2      The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support \par \par \uc2  the baht. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's outstanding foreign debt eased to $86.2 billion \par \par \uc2  at the end of 1998 from $93.4 billion at the end of 1997. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement that foreign debt \par \par \uc2  carried by the Thai private sector fell to $54.80 billion at \par \par \uc2  the end of December from $69.09 billion a year earlier. \par \par \uc2      *** In Hong Kong the forwards ticked up on the yuan worries \par \par \uc2  and there was some more bad economic news. \par \par \uc2      Retail sales fell 20 percent year-on-year in November in \par \par \uc2  terms of value and were down 17 percent in terms of volume. \par \par \uc2      *** The Koran won and Taiwan dollar were down in the line \par \par \uc2  with the wider market. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Change on the day MON 25 0923GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7998.......3.8000..........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......9285.00......8700.00.........-6.30% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.80........36.63.........-0.46% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.72........38.00.........-1.86% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6880.......1.6748.........-0.78% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.330.......32.210.........-0.37% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1178.00......1173.00.........-0.42% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....114.40.......113.75.........-0.57% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7998.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......9285.00......2432.00........-73.81% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.82........25.90........-29.66% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.72........26.50........-31.56% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6880.......1.4300........-15.28% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr..32.3300......27.7500........-14.17% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1178.00.......842.00........-28.52% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....114.40.......114.40..........0.00% \par \par \uc2   - Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3840 \par \par \uc2   - Email: asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv1p05zqb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
