\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals quiet but with firmer bias. \b0\par\par\uc2 651 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 1999\par 10:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0900 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were generally a \par \par \uc2  little firmer on the day with volume still quite low with \par \par \uc2  Indonesia and Malaysia still on holiday. \par \par \uc2      Some shed their earlier easy bias as the yen picked up on \par \par \uc2  the dollar. \par \par \uc2      But the dollar is expected to hold up well ahead of a key \par \par \uc2  speech by U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan. \par \par \uc2      *** The won stood out with a good gain despite a downturn \par \par \uc2  on the earlier firm Seoul stock market. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said state-run Export-Import Bank of Korea and \par \par \uc2  Korea Development Bank stepped into the market in an attempt to \par \par \uc2  rein in the won. \par \par \uc2      But sentiment was bullish after London rating agency Fitch \par \par \uc2  IBCA restored Korea's sovereign rating to investment grade. \par \par \uc2      On the back of what it called "an unprecedented recovery in \par \par \uc2  external liquidity," it upgraded Korea's long-term foreign \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating to BBB-minus from BB-plus and the short-term \par \par \uc2  foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating to F3 from B. \par \par \uc2  The long-term local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating remains unchanged at \par \par \uc2  A-minus, reflecting sharply higher public debt to fund \par \par \uc2  financial sector restructuring. \par \par \uc2      Korean jobs data showed unemployment running at 6.8 \par \par \uc2  percent, with 1.46 million unemployed at the end of last year. \par \par \uc2      The Labour Ministry saw the rate rising to 7.5 percent this \par \par \uc2  year and the government has set aside 7.69 trillion won for \par \par \uc2  unemployment benefits this year. \par \par \uc2      Unemployment was running at just two percent in 1997. \par \par \uc2      *** The Thai baht was little changed but there is room for \par \par \uc2  it to strengthen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2      The baht could find support if the Financial Sector \par \par \uc2  Restructuring Authority (FRA) goes ahead with another auction \par \par \uc2  of financial assets. \par \par \uc2      The FRA said on Tuesday that it was likely to hold another \par \par \uc2  auction of the assets seized from the 56 finance companies that \par \par \uc2  were closed down after the 1997 crisis. \par \par \uc2      They had a book value in March of 231 billion baht. \par \par \uc2      The Bank of Thailand reaffirmed its belief that market \par \par \uc2  forces and economic fundamentals should dictate the value of \par \par \uc2  the baht. \par \par \uc2      Governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul, told reporters the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to \par \par \uc2  protect the value of the baht in the past seven months. \par \par \uc2      "In the past seven months since I came to office, the Bank \par \par \uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market," he said. *** The \par \par \uc2  Singapore dollar was a little firmer. \par \par \uc2      Singapore non-oil domestic exports fell by 8.5 percent in \par \par \uc2  December from the same month a year earlier. \par \par \uc2      December non-oil domestic exports, which fell 6.6 percent \par \par \uc2  in November, totalled Singapore $7.74 billion. \par \par \uc2      Singapore's total trade fell 14.3 percent in December in \par \par \uc2  nominal terms. \par \par \uc2      The figures were much weaker than expected with a Reuters \par \par \uc2  poll this week predicting a nominal contraction in non-oil \par \par \uc2  domestic exports in December from a year earlier of 4.4 \par \par \uc2  percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Change on the day WED 20 0915GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7900.......3.8000.........0.26% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8440.00......8475.00.........0.41% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.47........36.45........-0.05% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.25........38.32.........0.18% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6790.......1.6820.........0.18% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.240.......32.245.........0.02% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1165.00......1174.10.........0.78% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....113.30.......114.00.........0.62% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7900.......2.5200........-33.51% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......8440.00......2432.00........-71.18% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.45........25.90........-28.94% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........38.25........26.50........-30.72% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6790.......1.4300........-14.83% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr..32.2400......27.7500........-13.93% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1165.00.......842.00........-27.73% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....113.30.......114.40..........0.97% \par \par \uc2   - Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3840 \par \par \uc2   - Email: asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba000002001090