\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA MARKETS - Korea making the grade. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Christopher Kaufman \par \uc2 1,159 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 1999\par 11:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      HONG KONG Jan 5, (Reuters) - Asian share markets were \par \par \uc2  volatile in thin post-holiday trade on Tuesday, with Korea and \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  leading gainers and Taiwan stumbling despite government \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained ground against the US dollar in \par \par \uc2  line with the Japanese yen's dramatic rally, although the \par \par \uc2  Singapore dollar defied the pull of the yen. \par \par \uc2      Sing dollar selling was said to be linked to purchases of \par \par \uc2  the Thai baht, as foreigners piled into the local stock market. \par \par \uc2      But volumes were very thin, and traders said there was \par \par \uc2  little in the way of fresh or significant factors to move the \par \par \uc2  market. \par \par \uc2      "There's no real volume going through," said a regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a European bank. \par \par \uc2      KOREAN STOCKS UP ON OUTLOOK UPGRADE \par \par \uc2      Korean shares moved ahead and spreads on outstanding U.S. \par \par \uc2  dollar bonds remained stiff after rising on the back of an \par \par \uc2  outlook upgrade from ratings agency Standard & Poor's. \par \par \uc2      During New York trading, S&P changed its outlook on South \par \par \uc2  Korea to "positive" from "stable" and affirmed the country's \par \par \uc2  local and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  credit ratings. \par \par \uc2      The improved outlook "has already led to a 20 basis point \par \par \uc2  rise in benchmark spreads both in Korea five year and ten year \par \par \uc2  bonds" said Paul Marshall, associate director of credit trading \par \par \uc2  at Barclays Capital in Hong Kong told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  "I think that the factors that have led to the rally in \par \par \uc2  Asian bonds over the last three months or so are still in \par \par \uc2  place," he said. \par \par \uc2  Marshall cited three key points as supporting dollar bonds \par \par \uc2  of Asian sovereigns in the first part of 1999: a weaker US \par \par \uc2  dollar, positive current account positions of regional \par \par \uc2  economies, and lower domestic interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Shares jumped on the news in Seoul, after having rallied \par \par \uc2  sharply throughout the last quarter on expectations the country \par \par \uc2  would soon climb out of the "junk" investment grade acquired at \par \par \uc2  the height of the Asia crisis. \par \par \uc2      Foreign investors were seen picking up leading blue chips \par \par \uc2  KEPCO and Korea Telecom. \par \par \uc2      But a strategist looking at the KOSPI index in Hong Kong \par \par \uc2  said investing in the market at current levels, having tested \par \par \uc2  the 600 point level repeatedly in the last two sessions, was \par \par \uc2  more an act of hope than a fundamental strategy. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON KEEPS PACE WITH YEN, \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  TALKS IT DOWN \par \par \uc2  Among Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Korean won kept closest pace \par \par \uc2  with the mighty yen, trading in a 30 won range and finishing out \par \par \uc2  the day near its highs. \par \par \uc2  Foreign inflows of funds looking to catch the rising stock \par \par \uc2  market combined with exporter dollar sales orders to drive the \par \par \uc2  won's rise, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  met some resistance against the \par \par \uc2  dollar on verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of Korea. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  checking of dollar positions \par \par \uc2  at foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  desks in Seoul, taking some wind out of the won's \par \par \uc2  sails. \par \par \uc2  But by the end of the day, it had kept pace with the yen, \par \par \uc2  gaining around the same amount as the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against \par \par \uc2  the dollar. \par \par \uc2  THAI STOCKS LEAP AS FOREIGNERS RUSH IN \par \par \uc2  Foreign funds fueled a frantic rally in Thai stocks, with \par \par \uc2  turnover relatively high and speculative plays in banking and \par \par \uc2  property issues among the favoured plays of retail investors. \par \par \uc2  Brokers said bank stocks were attracting attention ahead of \par \par \uc2  a deadline on formalising recapitalisation plans between the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities and commercial banks chiefs on January \par \par \uc2  15th. \par \par \uc2  The market started the day in an upbeat mood after Thai \par \par \uc2  Military Bank Plc announced last night it was cutting prime \par \par \uc2  rates by 50 basis points to 12 percent. \par \par \uc2      Expectations of further reductions in prime rates were seen \par \par \uc2  helping property shares head higher as well. \par \par \uc2      TAIWAN SHARES SELL DOWN AGAINST GOVERNMENT SUPPORT \par \par \uc2      Despite continued government support of Taiwan's asset \par \par \uc2  markets, stock investors sold the main index down sharply, \par \par \uc2  albeit in light volume. \par \par \uc2      The weighted index found itself at fresh 29-month lows at \par \par \uc2  the close, on its first day of trade in 1999. \par \par \uc2      Market turnover was described as "blah" by a Hong Kong \par \par \uc2  institutional sales trader, only reaching T$43.97 billion on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday against T$51.74 billion on December 31. \par \par \uc2      The trader said initial selling pressure began after falls \par \par \uc2  on Tokyo's Nikkei index and gathered steam in the latter part of \par \par \uc2  the session. \par \par \uc2      INDONESIA BUDGET SHOCKS NOBODY, MARKET SHRUGS BUT MOVES \par \par \uc2  AHEAD \par \par \uc2      Indonesian stocks gained toward the close after having \par \par \uc2  traded in lacklustre ranges through most of the session. \par \par \uc2      At midday, the market had a look at the country's draft \par \par \uc2  budget for 1999/2000, but was not inspired by the slow recovery \par \par \uc2  projections. \par \par \uc2      "It is not really a surprise," Sri Mulyani Indrawati, an \par \par \uc2  economist at the University of Indonesia in Jakarta, told \par \par \uc2  Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2      "This budget is not really functioning to stimulate the \par \par \uc2  economy," she said, suggesting the already battered financial \par \par \uc2  structure and devastated social networks still needed acute \par \par \uc2  attention. \par \par \uc2  By the close of business the Jakarta stock exchange had \par \par \uc2  moved higher in the post-holiday thin conditions by more than \par \par \uc2  3.6 percent. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2   Change on the day TUE 05 0943GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7999.......3.8000.........0.00% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......7825.00......7925.00.........1.28% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.03........36.12.........0.25% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........37.96........38.50.........1.42% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6630.......1.6560........-0.42% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6630.......1.6560........-0.42% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.130.......32.200.........0.22% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..