\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Little Changed Early; Mkt Fears Ctrl Bks \b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 1998\par 03:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--In early trading Friday morning, most Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are little changed from levels seen late in Asian hours the previous day, despite the overnight slide in the U.S. dollar against the yen. Only the Philippine peso (PHP) has strengthened significantly, rising to retest Thursday's highs against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  For the most part, traders attribute the relative heaviness of the Singapore dollar and the baht to the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to forestall excessive local-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation. \par \par \uc2  "There was huge (U.S. dollar) selling in the baht (market) yesterday," said a senior trader at a Thai bank. "Several hundred (million) dollars were sold, but the Bank of Thailand was on on the bid, buying and buying." \par \par \uc2  With the threat of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  still overshadowing the market, participants are wary of pushing the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rapidly higher. \par \par \uc2  At 0130 GMT (8:30 p.m. Thursday EST), the U.S. dollar is quoted against the baht (THB) at THB35.9200, down a little from THB35.9400 late Thursday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore will also enter the market to buy U.S. dollars at levels around S$1.6400 are weighing on the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  At present, the U.S. dollar is trading at S$1.6450, virtually unchanged from S$1.6449 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Still sidelined by most participants, the rupiah (IDR) is also barely moved, with the U.S. dollar quoted at IDR7,547, compared with IDR7,559 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  On the Philippine Dealing System, however, the U.S. dollar is at PHP38.77, up from its earlier low at PHP38.72, but down from PHP38.80 at Thursday's close. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 04-12-98 \par \par \uc2  0207GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duc401r54\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
