\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 -3:Baht Range-bound By  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 1998\par 11:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  As trading in the local market ended late Wednesday, the U.S. dollar was quoted at PHP39.020, down from PHP39.355 at the previous close. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in Southeast Asia, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lacked the peso's buoyancy. The Thai baht (THB), so frequently the star of recent sessions, crabbed sideways in a tight trading range throughout the Asian hours. \par \par \uc2  While most investors and traders retain a positive outlook for the baht, many are nervous of buying into the rally at this late stage. They are afraid that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market should the dollar fall below THB36.00, selling down the baht to take the pressure off local exporters. \par \par \uc2  Although Bank of Thailand Governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul declared on Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't attempting to prop up the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the THB36.00 level, he admitted that the bank had been buying dollars in the market. The purchases, he said, were aimed at acquiring dollars to settle the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's outstanding forward contracts, which amounted to $7.7 billion late last month. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asian trading Wednesday, the U.S. dollar was quoted at THB36.0300, down slightly from THB36.0650 late the previous day. \par \par \uc2  In general, however, most offshore investors are relatively bullish on the baht. Many are predicting further gains in December, with the Financial Sector Restructuring Authority's planned Dec. 15 auction of $1 billion worth of defunct financial companies assets attracting considerable foreign interest. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 02-12-98 \par \par \uc2  1031GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duc201o4q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
