\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals steady as dlr drifts lower. \b0\par\par\uc2 902 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1998\par 10:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0920 GMT - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were little changed but off \par \par \uc2  their lows in late trade as the dollar lost some of its shine \par \par \uc2  against the yen and mark. \par \par \uc2      The dollar's failure to break convincingly above 124 yen \par \par \uc2  overnight limited its rise, but dealers said its base was \par \par \uc2  supported by news that a mid-sized Japanese general contractor \par \par \uc2  JDC Corp had filed for bankruptcy protection. \par \par \uc2  *** Malaysian Second Finance Minister Mustapa Mohamed said \par \par \uc2  the government may tap overseas funds to help in the \par \par \uc2  restructuring and recapitalisation of domestic banks. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara governor Ali Abul Hassan Sulaiman said the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to promote bank mergers and would \par \par \uc2  soon launch a plan to chart the industry's direction over the \par \par \uc2  next two decades. \par \par \uc2  He also said Malaysia would not resort to printing money to \par \par \uc2  fund the fiscal deficit and would keep the fiscal shortfall at \par \par \uc2  six percent of GNP. \par \par \uc2  The IMF praised Malaysia's open trade regime as exceptional \par \par \uc2  by regional standards, but said the country's capital controls \par \par \uc2  could backfire, leaving the country vulnerable if its export \par \par \uc2  markets begin to dry up. \par \par \uc2  *** The rupiah was a bit lower but still doing well as the \par \par \uc2  conversion of aid dollars into the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to \par \par \uc2  provide support. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia governor Syahril Sabirin said there was room \par \par \uc2  for the rupiah to strengthen to a level just below 7,000 or to \par \par \uc2  6,500, while interest rates could slide towards 20-30 percent \par \par \uc2  over the next few months, barring major shocks. \par \par \uc2  The IMF is likely to debate the release of more cash for \par \par \uc2  Indonesia in mid-December after scheduling problems forced a \par \par \uc2  change to earlier plans. \par \par \uc2  The IMF board had earlier expected to discuss new payments \par \par \uc2  to both Indonesia and South Korea on Dec. 2, the date also set \par \par \uc2  to debate a $41 billion rescue package for Brazil. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia expects to receive $960 million from a $11.1 \par \par \uc2  billion loan approved just over a year ago and topped up in \par \par \uc2  August. \par \par \uc2  President B.J. Habibie and the country's religious leaders \par \par \uc2  pleaded for an end to sectarian violence after Christian mobs \par \par \uc2  torched and ransacked mosques in the remote eastern town of \par \par \uc2  Kupang. \par \par \uc2      *** The won held on to its gains as the yen strengthened \par \par \uc2  and exporters unloaded dollars. \par \par \uc2      Korea's trade surplus rose to $3.67 billion in November \par \par \uc2  from a $124 million surplus a year ago, according to \par \par \uc2  provisional data. \par \par \uc2      The won's firmer tone of late has helped on the inflation \par \par \uc2  front, with the government reporting that import and export \par \par \uc2  prices dropped in November from the previous month in won \par \par \uc2  terms. \par \par \uc2      November export prices fell 4.1 percent month on month but \par \par \uc2  were up 16.4 percent year on year. \par \par \uc2      November import prices fell 3.9 percent with the year on \par \par \uc2  year rate at up 15.3 percent. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said export prices of leather goods, \par \par \uc2  petrochemical and rubber products fell the most. \par \par \uc2      *** The Philippine peso was steady, supported by \par \par \uc2  remittances from overseas contract workers over the long \par \par \uc2  weekend. \par \par \uc2      The market was unaffected by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight \par \par \uc2  rate cuts as the bank said it would accept special peso \par \par \uc2  deposits at rates higher than the reverse repos. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut overnight rates by 12.5 basis points \par \par \uc2  each, leaving the overnight borrowing rate at 13.375 percent \par \par \uc2  and the lending rate at 15.375 percent. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last cut overnight rates by 25 basis \par \par \uc2  points on November 24. \par \par \uc2      Finance Secretary Edgardo Espiritu said the Philippines \par \par \uc2  would float a Samurai bond worth about $500 million to $1 \par \par \uc2  billion in January and the Japanese government had committed to \par \par \uc2  buy 50 percent of the issue. \par \par \uc2  *** The Thai baht was still stuck near the 36 per dollar \par \par \uc2  level amid shrinking volumes as traders worried about possible \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's consumer price index rose 4.7 percent \par \par \uc2  year-on-year in November against a 5.9 percent rise in October. \par \par \uc2      The Thai economy is expected to grow by one percent next \par \par \uc2  year against a sharp seven to eight percent contraction seen \par \par \uc2  this year, according to a government document agreed with the \par \par \uc2  IMF. \par \par \uc2  The IMF gave a green light to Thailand to widen the 1998/99 \par \par \uc2  budget deficit to five percent of GDP, but economists said this \par \par \uc2  would have a limited impact amid expectations of a steep fall \par \par \uc2  in farm sector income due to low commodity prices and a firming \par \par \uc2  baht. Change on the day \par \par \uc2  Change on the day TUE 01 0929GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7997.......3.8000..........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......7375.00......7350.00.........-0.34% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.03........36.05..........0.06% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........39.28........39.25.........-0.08% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6443.......1.6527..........0.51% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.390.......32.390..........0.00% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1243.00......1245.00..........0.16% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....122.56.......123.75..........0.97% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7997.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......7375.00......2432.00........-67.02% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.00........25.90........-28.06% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........39.28........26.50........-32.54% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6443.......1.4300........-13.03% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr..32.3900......27.7500........-14.33% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1243.00.......842.00........-32.26% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....122.56.......114.40.........-6.66% \par \par \uc2   - Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3840 \par \par \uc2   - Email: asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926duc103c54\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
