\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 : Baht Rises Early; Singapore Dlr Falls \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 1998\par 03:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht has strengthened in early trading in Southeast Asia Friday to retest its 58-week high set Thursday afternoon. The Singapore dollar, however, has sunk, with the U.S. dollar rising to test the S$1.65 level. \par \par \uc2  Continued U.S. dollar sales by investors accumulating baht (THB) in preparation for next month's Financial Sector Restructuring Authority asset auction have again pushed the U.S. dollar down through the THB36.00 level early Friday. \par \par \uc2  Should the current level of inflows persist until the auction date, the U.S. dollar could fall to as low as THB35.00 over the coming weeks, according to the senior dealer at one Thai bank. \par \par \uc2  Fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  have receded, he explained, after officials on Thursday emphasized that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not attempt to fly in the face of market trends. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will buy the dollars it needs, but it will not try to push the market up," he said. \par \par \uc2  At 0225 GMT (9:25 p.m. Thursday EST) the U.S. dollar is quoted at THB35.99, down from THB36.02 late in Asian trading the previous day. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, against the Singapore dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen sharply in early trading, to break up through S$1.65. \par \par \uc2  "There is a very real possibility we will see the (U.S.) dollar up at S$1.66 soon," said a senior treasury executive at a Singapore bank. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is being pushed upward as foreign institutions book and convert their profits from the recent run-up in the local stock market. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 27-11-98 \par \par \uc2  0239GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917dubr01knj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
