\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals hold up as Moody's hits yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 848 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 1998\par 05:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0435 GMT - Most Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held their ground \par \par \uc2  despite the yen's losses after Moody's Investors Service \par \par \uc2  downgraded Japan's sovereign debt rating. \par \par \uc2      Moody's lowered Japan's yen-denominated debt and \par \par \uc2  foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt ratings to Aa1 from Aaa, citing weakness \par \par \uc2  in the country's fiscal standing and financial system. \par \par \uc2      Active short-covering after the Moody's move pushed the \par \par \uc2  dollar as high as 122.35 yen, up over two yen from its early \par \par \uc2  lows, but dealers said further gains were capped by caution \par \par \uc2  ahead of the Federal Reserve's policy meeting tonight. \par \par \uc2  Most market participants are looking for a quarter point \par \par \uc2  cut in the Fed funds rate, and this has kept Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \par \par \uc2  stock markets well supported in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2  But some dealers felt the Fed might decide to hold off for \par \par \uc2  analysisthe time being as the U.S. economy has been looking \par \par \uc2  fairly healthy. \par \par \uc2  "It depends on what they think is most important now. If \par \par \uc2  they want to keep the recovery in emerging markets going, they \par \par \uc2  should cut rates," said a European bank dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2      *** The impact of the Moody's move was also cushioned by \par \par \uc2  the fact that it had been widely expected for some time. \par \par \uc2      "The ratings agencies are always behind the curve...They \par \par \uc2  should have done this when Japan went into recession. Now \par \par \uc2  things are turning for the better and they cut the ratings," \par \par \uc2  the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said substantially reduced speculative activity and \par \par \uc2  year-end position squaring were also tempering the impact of \par \par \uc2  any bad news for regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  *** The Thai baht extended its recent gains despite news \par \par \uc2  the country's largest refiner, Thai Oil, had defaulted on \par \par \uc2  interest as well as principle payments on $1.85 billion worth \par \par \uc2  of debt. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers attributed the baht's resilience to demand \par \par \uc2  from foreigners ahead of the government's December 2 auction of \par \par \uc2  401 billion baht of defunct finance company assets. \par \par \uc2  But the baht's rise was limited by fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent too sharp an appreciation, which \par \par \uc2  could hurt \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  *** The Singapore dollar was again worst hit by the yen's \par \par \uc2  fall, with dealers increasingly convinced that local \par \par \uc2  authorities were not in favour of it strengthening beyond the \par \par \uc2  1.62 level. \par \par \uc2  *** The Philippine peso remained on a firm footing after \par \par \uc2  climbing above the 40 per dollar level in early trade, buoyed \par \par \uc2  by hopes of a U.S. rate cut and remittances by Filipinos \par \par \uc2  working abroad. \par \par \uc2       Dollar bids from interbank players were expected to block \par \par \uc2  the peso's rally near the 39.50 level. \par \par \uc2      The Philippines posted a $332 million merchandise trade \par \par \uc2  surplus in September compared with a deficit of $619 million \par \par \uc2  the year before. Exports rose 19 percent year-on-year while \par \par \uc2  imports fell nearly 17 percent. \par \par \uc2  *** U.S. Vice President Al Gore played on Malaysian \par \par \uc2  sensitivities again by repeating that democracy and freedom \par \par \uc2  were essential for economic reform. \par \par \uc2  Gore, who is representing President Bill Clinton at the \par \par \uc2  APEC summit in Kuala Lumpur, infuriated Malaysia on Monday by \par \par \uc2  saluting the "brave people" supporting an anti-government \par \par \uc2  movement started by detained former deputy prime minister Anwar \par \par \uc2  Ibrahim. \par \par \uc2  His blunt words, later backed by Clinton, drew swift and \par \par \uc2  biting condemnation from Malaysian officials and business \par \par \uc2  leaders. \par \par \uc2  Malaysia's discomfiture was compounded when Philippine \par \par \uc2  President Joseph Estrada met Anwar's wife in a show of support \par \par \uc2  for the sacked minister and a rebuke to Mahathir. \par \par \uc2  *** The U.S. and Japan unveiled a $10 billion aid plan for \par \par \uc2  Asia at the APEC meeting. The package comprises a combined $5 \par \par \uc2  billion from Japan, the Asian Development Bank and the World \par \par \uc2  Bank. With a further $5 billion from the U.S. through Export \par \par \uc2  Import Bank trade financing and Overseas Private Investment \par \par \uc2  Corp programmes. \par \par \uc2      In addition the U.S. will provide an additional $1 billion \par \par \uc2  in trade financing each to Indonesia, Thailand and South Korea. \par \par \uc2      A senior Japanese official said the $10 billion aid plan \par \par \uc2  was separate from Japan's $30 billion Miyazawa plan for Asia, \par \par \uc2  although some of the ideas were similar and overlapped. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2   Change on the day TUE 17 0439GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid...