\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals up as yen shrugs off Moody's. \b0\par\par\uc2 912 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 1998\par 10:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0900 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed in late trade \par \par \uc2  as the yen bounced back from its lows despite Moody's Investors \par \par \uc2  Service downgrade of Japan's sovereign debt rating. \par \par \uc2      It fell to a low of 122.35 to the dollar after Moody's \par \par \uc2  lowered Japan's yen-denominated debt and foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt \par \par \uc2  ratings to Aa1 from Aaa, citing weakness in the country's \par \par \uc2  fiscal standing and financial system. \par \par \uc2  But growing hopes of a U.S. rate cut and Bank of Japan \par \par \uc2  governor Masaru Hayami's comment that the strong yen would help \par \par \uc2  Asian exports to Japan dragged the dollar back down. \par \par \uc2  Most market participants are looking for a quarter point \par \par \uc2  cut in the Fed funds rate, and this has kept Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \par \par \uc2  stock markets well supported in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2  But some dealers felt the Fed might decide to hold off for \par \par \uc2  the time being as the U.S. economy has been looking fairly \par \par \uc2  healthy. \par \par \uc2  "It depends on what they think is most important now. If \par \par \uc2  they want to keep the recovery in emerging markets going, they \par \par \uc2  should cut rates," said a European bank dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2      *** The impact of the Moody's move was also cushioned by \par \par \uc2  the fact that it had been widely expected for some time. \par \par \uc2      "The ratings agencies are always behind the curve...They \par \par \uc2  should have done this when Japan went into recession. Now \par \par \uc2  things are turning for the better and they cut the ratings," \par \par \uc2  the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said substantially reduced speculative activity and \par \par \uc2  year-end position squaring were also tempering the impact of \par \par \uc2  any bad news for regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  *** Indonesian markets were closed for a religious holiday \par \par \uc2  but the rupiah edged up in thin offshore trade after IMF Asia \par \par \uc2  Pacific Director Hubert Neiss said he saw room for the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent appreciation to continue. \par \par \uc2  Neiss also told Reuters Television that international \par \par \uc2  confidence in Indonesia would falter if political violence and \par \par \uc2  rioting persisted. \par \par \uc2  He said the recent unrest in Jakarta did not invalidate the \par \par \uc2  latest IMF letter of intent with the country. The letter \par \par \uc2  forecast a budget deficit of six percent of GDP in the fiscal \par \par \uc2  year to end March, a GDP contraction of upto 15 percent in 1998 \par \par \uc2  and inflation within the 80 percent target. \par \par \uc2  *** The Thai baht extended its recent gains despite news \par \par \uc2  the country's largest refiner, Thai Oil, had defaulted on \par \par \uc2  interest as well as principle payments on $1.85 billion worth \par \par \uc2  of debt. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers attributed the baht's resilience to demand \par \par \uc2  from foreigners ahead of the government's December 2 auction of \par \par \uc2  401 billion baht of defunct finance company assets. \par \par \uc2  But the baht's rise was limited by fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent too sharp an appreciation, which \par \par \uc2  could hurt \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  *** The Philippine peso held above the 40 per dollar level, \par \par \uc2  buoyed by hopes of a U.S. rate cut and remittances by Filipinos \par \par \uc2  working abroad. \par \par \uc2  The Philippines posted a $332 million merchandise trade \par \par \uc2  surplus in September compared with a deficit of $619 million \par \par \uc2  the year before. \par \par \uc2  Exports rose 19 percent year-on-year while imports fell \par \par \uc2  nearly 17 percent, suggesting that export growth could soon \par \par \uc2  slow as imports of raw materials to produce export goods were \par \par \uc2  falling. \par \par \uc2  *** The official agenda of the annual APEC summit was \par \par \uc2  sidelined by a growing diplomatic row between the U.S. and \par \par \uc2  Malaysia after Vice President Al Gore repeated that democracy \par \par \uc2  and freedom were essential for economic reform. \par \par \uc2  Gore, who is representing President Bill Clinton at the \par \par \uc2  APEC summit in Kuala Lumpur, infuriated Malaysia on Monday by \par \par \uc2  saluting the "brave people" supporting an anti-government \par \par \uc2  movement started by detained former deputy prime minister Anwar \par \par \uc2  Ibrahim. \par \par \uc2  His blunt words, later backed by Clinton, drew swift and \par \par \uc2  biting condemnation from Malaysian officials, including Foreign \par \par \uc2  Minister Abdullah Badawi who accused Gore of inciting \par \par \uc2  lawlessness and interfering in the internal affairs of another \par \par \uc2  country. \par \par \uc2  *** Analysts welcomed a joint U.S.-Japan $10 billion aid \par \par \uc2  plan for Asia unveiled at the meeting, as a welcome step but \par \par \uc2  said it was too small to counter the region's credit crunch. \par \par \uc2  The plan comprises a combined $5 billion from Japan, the \par \par \uc2  Asian Development Bank and the World Bank and a further $5 \par \par \uc2  billion from the U.S. through trade financing and Overseas \par \par \uc2  Private Investment Corp programmes. \par \par \uc2  The IMF's Neiss said the new aid, coupled with Japan's $30 \par \par \uc2  billion Miyazawa plan, would have a substantial economic impact \par \par \uc2  on the region. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2   Change on the day TUE 17 0856GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7997.......3.8000.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......7450.00......7600.00.........2.01% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.25........36.45.........0.55% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........39.80........40.00.........0.50% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6312.......1.6355.........0.26% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.475.......32.550.........0.23% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1303.00......1313.20.........0.78% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....120.00.......121.15.........0.96% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7997.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......7450.00......2432.00........-67.36% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.25........25.90........-28.55% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........39.80........26.50........-33.42% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6312.......1.4300........-12.33% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr..32.4750......27.7500........-14.55% \par \par \uc2   Korean won..1303.00.......842.00........-35.38% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....120.00.......114.40.........-4.67% \par \par \uc2   - Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3840 \par \par \uc2   - Email: asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dubh04bpr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\