\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -3: Baht Seen Resilient In Longer Term \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 1998\par 10:26\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Most resilient of the Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to any renewed sell-off will be the Thai baht, say analysts, applauding the Bangkok government's progress towards economic and financial restructuring. \par \par \uc2  That does not mean the baht is destined to push still higher, however, after rising around 15% in the last four months. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , already actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to moderate the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise will step in to prevent the U.S. dollar falling below the THB35.00 level say many analysts and traders. \par \par \uc2  "It is not in the government's interest to see the baht strengthen further," says Wong at DKB, who argues that the Thai authorities are anxious to preserve export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  "They don't want to jeopardize the only sector of the economy that is growing," said Wong, adding that unless signs of an export slowdown appear, the Bank of Thailand is "comfortable" to see the U.S. dollar trading between THB35.00 and THB40.00. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asian dealing on Friday, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at THB36.51, up a fraction from THB36.40 towards the end of trading on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar also fell back a touch on Friday, as market rumors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was buying U.S. dollars spooked traders into hastily covering their short positions in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Late in Asian trading the U.S. dollar was being quoted at S$1.6286, up slightly from S$1.6239 at the same time the previous day. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  11-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0426EST \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916dub602mbh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
