\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Thailand \highlight\uc2  says won't  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to move baht. \b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 1998\par 06:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Oct 30 (Reuters) - Thai Prime Minister Chuan Leekpai said on Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to affect the level of the baht. \par \par \uc2  Chuan told reporters his government did not have a specific view on the appropriate level for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has risen strongly against the U.S. dollar in recent days. He said the level of the baht would be set by the market. \par \par \uc2  "It is difficult to tell if the baht at this level is appropriate," Chuan said, adding that the market should decide the level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We cannot oblige calls by some exporters for government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (to sell baht) as it would distort the market. The baht should find its own market level," Chuan said. \par \par \uc2  "The baht's rally has not been due to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it's moved in line with market forces," he said. \par \par \uc2  The prime minister said the recent strength of the baht was mostly due to inflows of funds into the country. \par \par \uc2  The baht stood at 36.70/36.80 to the dollar at 0515 GMT on Friday, not far off the 12-month high of 36.66 that was traded on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was devalued from around 25 to the dollar in July last year and fell to an all-time low of 56.90 in January before beginning to rally. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand has bought dollars for baht at least once this week but the action may have only been to mop up cheap dollars to clear forward \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap obligations, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers say. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul said on Wednesday that the Bank of Thailand's net forward swap obligations had fallen in recent days, a change which dealers attribute to buying of dollars for baht. \par \par \uc2  Chuan said there was no clear-cut impact of the stronger baht on the country's export sector. \par \par \uc2  "The baht's gains do not affect Thai exports (much) because other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have also appreciated. We may lose some of the U.S. market because of the dollar weakness." \par \par \uc2  - Bangkok Newsroom (662) 253-5000 ext 410 \par \par \uc2  - e-mail: rtrburo@ksc15.th.com reuters crj. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926duau05oc3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
