\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Stronger Mid-Morning On Continuing Dlr Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 1998\par 04:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht (THB) is stronger in mid-morning Asian trade Thursday, with gains expected to continue but at a slower pace than Wednesday, dealers say. \par \par \uc2  At 0255 GMT (9:55 p.m. EST Wednesday), the dollar traded at THB36.665, down from Wednesday's close of THB36.85. The dollar last closed below THB36.70 Oct. 16, 1997. \par \par \uc2  General dollar weakness remains the primary factor behind the baht's rise, dealers say. The dollar has been under pressure around the world this week on worries over Brazil's economy, because of heavy U.S. investment exposure there. \par \par \uc2  A local market factor pushing down the dollar is the Bank of Thailand's order to Thai commercial banks earlier this month to reduce their foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  asset holdings to 15% of Tier 1 capital, from 20%, effective November. \par \par \uc2  "It's a good reason for banks to sell U.S. dollars right now," says a dealer at Bangkok Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a French bank in Bangkok says Thai Farmers Bank, the nation's third largest commercial bank, started selling dollars last week to comply with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  order. \par \par \uc2  Market participants say \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which Tuesday said it has bought dollars to moderate the baht's rise and to settle swap contracts, could stem further gains. \par \par \uc2  Dealers are split about the likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A dealer at a U.S. bank in Singapore says that at THB36.60 to THB36.70, agent banks could buy dollars to brake the baht's rise. \par \par \uc2  The Bangkok Bank dealer dismisses \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk. "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't been seen lately, and they're not coming in today. We were expecting them at THB37, and they didn't come in at all," he says. \par \par \uc2  Dealers see the dollar weakening to THB36.50 in Thursday trade. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 29-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0312GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duat00m5x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
