\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKETS  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - S.E. Asia surges. \b0\par\par\uc2 585 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 1998\par 14:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 27 (Reuters) - South east Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  surged on Tuesday, boosted largely by local inflows, but the yen's steady softening against the dollar pulled the South Korean won down in its wake, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The major central European units remained solid, with the Czech crown maintaining its strength despite Monday's larger than expected interest rate cut. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso led the Asian winners, with dollar/peso dropping nearly two percent from New York closing levels. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was lifted mainly by seasonal inflows as Philippine workers overseas remitted their earnings, as well as local press reports that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not move immediately to cap the peso rise. \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's volatile rupiah notched up a further strong gain, supported by expectations of another disbursement next month from the International Monetary Fund, analysts added. \par \par \uc2  The baht also continued to firm as Thailand remained a favourite with investors cautiously eyeing a return to Asia. \par \par \uc2  "The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been trying to no avail to prevent the baht from appreciating as sentiment remains positive," analysts at Standard Chartered said in a note to clients. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to buy dollars, in an effort to stabilise the baht's ascent. \par \par \uc2  Taiwan's dollar eased back slightly from a seven-month high of 32.565 against the dollar, seen during the Asian day, and analysts said strong foreign interest in Taiwanese stocks was underpinning demand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the South Korean won, which like most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has seen a run of strength this month on the back of the yen's sudden rise against the dollar, lost ground as dollar/yen edged further towards 120. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said South Korea's fundamentals remained shaky, with unconvincing talk that its dominant business empires would be restructured, and a weakening yen would eat into the country's export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  "Domestically they're in a real mess," said Graham Neilson, an Asia economist at Banque Paribas in London. "The won needs to go weaker against the dollar and everything else, to see at least some benefit to the export sector." \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown held onto the gains it made after Monday's interest rate cuts, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sliced 100 basis points off the key two-week repo rate. \par \par \uc2  "(The cut) was much more than the market was looking for and the crown firmed on the back of it, which is amazingly counterintuitive," said Jake Moore, an emerging markets analyst at Barclays Capital in London. \par \par \uc2  "But it's got to be good news for the economy and good news for investment, so it has remained fairly stable." \par \par \uc2  The zloty firmed slightly ahead of a meeting on Wednesday of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Council, amid expectations that the decision-making body might cut Polish interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "It still remains the most attractive Eastern European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in terms of yield, so investors are still looking to buy up Treasury bills and short-term interest rate instruments," Moore said. \par \par \uc2  Hungary's forint, normally the most fragile of the main central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trio, rose sharply against its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket as foreign investors bought into Hungarian stocks and other assets. \par \par \uc2  By the end of morning trade in Budapest the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 1.2 percent below basket parity compared with 1.6 percent below at Monday's close, well within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4.5 percent wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113duar02qoc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
