\par\par \b \uc2  Exotic Focus/Baht -2: Foreign Investment Adds Strength \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 1998\par 09:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  While the baht has risen steadily since the dollar touched an all-time high of THB56.45 Jan. 12, it remains 32% below its close June 30, 1997, the last trading day before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Thailand's float of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  July 2 sparked the Asian economic crisis. \par \par \uc2  But the baht's recent rise has also brought concerns that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be becoming too strong. Thailand needs strong export growth to stabilize its economy, and undue \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength could jeopardize that. \par \par \uc2  Chatu Mongol said Oct. 16 that if the Bank of Thailand hadn't acted in recent weeks, the baht would be even stronger. He declined to characterize the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's actions as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains committed to allowing the market to determine the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value. \par \par \uc2  Previously, he has said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars to settle forward foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  contracts. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably is buying and selling to moderate dollar/baht movement. The government wouldn't want too strong a baht, says Citibank's Lam, expecting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bidding if the dollar falls below THB35 in the near term. \par \par \uc2  Analysts are circling Dec. 2 on their calendars for the next key sign of investor attitudes toward Thailand's economic fortunes. On that date, the government's Financial Sector Restructuring Authority will auction some THB400 billion of assets from the 56 failed finance companies the government shut down in December 1997. \par \par \uc2  "Thailand is one of the first countries in Asia to do much restructuring," says Citibank's Lam. "If the auction goes well, it will be a sign of renewed confidence, and could pave the way for recovery." \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 22-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0711GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duam00cp6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
